52ed4a4a-e8ca-4a13-a5da-aea42e9055bd,41ac740a-c2c9-4612-80b6-2b27ef85c198,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.doi,dc.identifier.scopusid,dc.identifier.uri,dc.identifier.wosid",identifier_conflict,"[""52ed4a4a-e8ca-4a13-a5da-aea42e9055bd"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Benguria Donoso, Rafael||Depassier Terán, María Cristina||Benguria, RD||Depassier, MC"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2017-04-25T19:23:58Z||2021-07-23T03:38:22Z"", """", ""2017-04-25T19:23:58Z||2021-07-23T03:38:22Z"", """", """", """", """", ""1996"", """", """", """", """", """", ""We consider the Brezis-Nirenberg problem for the Laplacian with a singular drift for a (geodesic) ball in both R-n and S-n, 3 <= n <= 5. The singular drift we consider derives from a potential which is symmetric around the center of the (geodesic) ball. Here the potential is given by a parameter (delta say) times the logarithm of the distance to the center of the ball. In both cases we determine the exact region in the parameter space for which positive smooth solutions of this problem exist and the exact region for which there are no solutions. The parameter space is characterized by the (geodesic) radius of the ball, delta, and lambda, the coupling constant of the linear term of the Brezis-Nirenberg problem. (C) 2017 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.||We consider the bifurcation problem u '' + lambda u = N(u) with two point boundary conditions where N(LI) is a general nonlinear term which may also depend on the eigenvalue lambda. We give a variational characterization of the bifurcating branch lambda as a function of th amplitude of the solution. As an application we show how it can be used to obtain simple approximate closed formulas for the period of large amplitude oscillations."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""4"", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC||WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1016/j.na.2017.03.006"", """", """", """", ""1079-7114"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0031-9007"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85018507626"", """", ""https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.77.2847||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/264590"", """", ""WOS:000401126800010"", """", ""INSTITUTO DE FÍSICA;BENGURIA DONOSO RAFAEL JOSE URBANO;S/I;99598||INSTITUTO DE FÍSICA;DEPASSIER TERAN MARIA CRISTINA;S/I;99694"", """", ""14"", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2850"", """", ""2847"", """", """", """", """", """", ""AMERICAN PHYSICAL SOC"", """", """", ""Physical Review Letters Vol. 77, no. 14 (1996), p. [2847]-2850"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Physical Review Letters"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Variational Principle for Eigenvalue Problems of Hamiltonian System||Variational principle for eigenvalue problems of Hamiltonian systems"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Variational Principle for Eigenvalue Problems of Hamiltonian System||Variational principle for eigenvalue problems of Hamiltonian systems"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""77"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""99598||99694"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-07-26;99598;1||2021-07-26;99694;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""25768"", """", """", """", ""02e1ca63-9901-4100-9518-20e4c3c3cad8"", """", """", ""ISI-1990-1991-1992-1994-1996-1997-1998-1999-2000-2002-2003-2004-2005-2006-2007-2008-2009-2010-2011-2012-2013-2014-2015-2016-2017-2018||Scopus-2010-2011-2012-2013-2014-2015-2016-2017-2018||WOS||Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC;25-04-2017||WOS;05-06-2021"", """", """", ""Validado||Sin validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", ""Unpaywall"", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2021-07-26;99598;1||2021-07-26;99694;1"", """"]","[""41ac740a-c2c9-4612-80b6-2b27ef85c198"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Benguria, RD||Depassier, MC"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-07-23T03:38:22Z"", """", ""2021-07-23T03:38:22Z"", """", """", """", """", ""1996"", """", """", """", """", """", ""We consider the bifurcation problem u '' + lambda u = N(u) with two point boundary conditions where N(LI) is a general nonlinear term which may also depend on the eigenvalue lambda. We give a variational characterization of the bifurcating branch lambda as a function of th amplitude of the solution. As an application we show how it can be used to obtain simple approximate closed formulas for the period of large amplitude oscillations."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""4"", """", """", """", ""WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1103/PhysRevLett.77.2847"", """", """", """", ""1079-7114"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0031-9007"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:0006979411"", """", ""https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.77.2847||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/258846"", """", ""WOS:A1996VJ72300001"", """", """", """", ""14"", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2850"", """", ""2847"", """", """", """", """", """", ""AMERICAN PHYSICAL SOC"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""PHYSICAL REVIEW LETTERS"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Variation