c0d3265b-77e4-4257-bb2f-ebf53e44f695,443fcd98-4622-4a98-914d-79285c86c2c3,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.issn,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""c0d3265b-77e4-4257-bb2f-ebf53e44f695"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""carga"", """", """", """", """", ""Otero, Rodrigo A.||Soto-Acuna, Sergio||Ugalde, Raul||Vargas, Alexander O.||Otero R.A.||Soto-Acuna S.||Ugalde R.||Vargas A.O."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-08-09T12:33:04Z||2026-08-16T12:35:05Z"", """", ""2026-08-09T12:33:04Z||2026-08-16T12:35:05Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2026"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Two isolated bones of sea turtles from Algarrobo, in central Chile, are described. A fragment of a flat element of Ypresian age is identified as part of a right hypoplastron, referable to an indeterminate Pan-Chelonioidea. A second, large fragment from middle-to-upper Eocene levels belonging to the second or fourth left costal of a carapace, preserves distinctive features such as a considerable uniform thickness (5-7 mm), and a prominent ventral rib ridge, plus scute sulci remarkably similar to extant Cheloniidae such as Chelonia mydas or Lepidochelys spp. Based on these features, it is identified as an indeterminate Pan-Cheloniidae. The studied material represents the first occurrences of sea turtles in the Eocene of central Chile. The different ages of the specimens show the persistence of taxa related to Pan-Chelonioidea throughout the Eocene in the southeastern Pacific, helping to fill the austral geographic gap of the group during the Paleogene.||© 2026, Servicio Nacional de Geologia y Mineria. All rights reserved.Two isolated bones of sea turtles from Algarrobo, in central Chile, are described. A fragment of a flat element of Ypresian age is identified as part of a right hypoplastron, referable to an indeterminate Pan-Chelonioidea. A second, large fragment from middle-to-upper Eocene levels belonging to the second or fourth left costal of a carapace, preserves distinctive features such as a considerable uniform thickness (5-7 mm), and a prominent ventral rib ridge, plus scute sulci remarkably similar to extant Cheloniidae such as Chelonia mydas or Lepidochelys spp. Based on these features, it is identified as an indeterminate Pan-Cheloniidae. The studied material represents the first occurrences of sea turtles in the Eocene of central Chile. The different ages of the specimens show the persistence of taxa related to Pan-Chelonioidea throughout the Eocene in the southeastern Pacific, helping to fill the austral geographic gap of the group during the Paleogene."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS||SCOPUS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.5027/andgeoV53n2-3874"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""0718-7106"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105046031666"", """", ""https://doi.org/10.5027/andgeoV53n2-3874||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/424918"", """", ""WOS:001824405500013"", """", """", """", ""2"", """", """", ""en||eng"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""407"", """", ""399"", """", """", """", """", """", ""SERVICIO NACIONAL GEOLOGIA MINERVA||Servicio Nacional de Geologia y Mineria"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""ANDEAN GEOLOGY"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Testudines||South Pacific||Paleogene||Southern Hemisphere||Weddellian Province"", """", """", """", """", ""First sea turtle remains (Pan-Chelonioidea) from the Eocene of Algarrobo, central Chile||First sea turtle remains (Pan-Chelonioidea) from the Eocene of Algarrobo, central ChilePrimeros restos de tor