""", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1103/physreve.59.4889"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""0129-055X"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:4243700211"", """", ""https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/260521||https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X9400033X"", """", ""WOS:000080382700029"", """", ""INSTITUTO DE FÍSICA;BENGURIA DONOSO RAFAEL JOSE URBANO;S/I;99598"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Reviews in Mathematical Physics. Vol. 6, no. 0 (1994), p. [999]-1009"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Reviews in Mathematical Physics"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""The Range of Values of 2/1 and 3/1 for the Fixed Membrane Problem"", """", """", """", """", """", ""The Range of Values of 2/1 and 3/1 for the Fixed Membrane Problem"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""99598"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-07-26;99598;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""25282"", """", """", """", ""29ae3104-1143-4a45-afe8-9bb3e47bd237"", """", """", ""WOS||ISI||Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC;10-04-2017"", """", """", ""Validado"", """", """", """", ""Unpaywall"", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2021-07-26;99598;1"", """"]"
1ec1869a-eead-4e19-b242-1fecedbf44ac,c20e36e8-788a-4d5a-8983-3a9fac973002,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""1ec1869a-eead-4e19-b242-1fecedbf44ac"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""carga"", """", """", """", """", ""Borchert Billik, Evelyn||Lema, Guillermo||Springmüller P., Daniel||González Casanova, Katia Angelina||Chang, Win T.||González Foretic, Rodrigo Vicente||Garay Greve, Francisco Javier||Borchert E||Lema G||Springmuller D||González K||Chang WT||González R||Garay F"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-05-24T20:26:17Z||2026-05-04T12:54:19Z"", """", ""2021-05-24T20:26:17Z||2026-05-04T12:54:19Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2015"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Aortic aneurysms (AA) in the paediatric population are uncommon. The use of umbilical catheters in neonates has been associated with infections and, on some occasions, the formation of aortic aneurysms. The surgical repair of these aneurysms is one type of treatment; however, percutaneous intervention with stents could provide an alternative treatment route, with fewer complications.||The aim of this report is to present the therapeutic scope of a hybrid procedure, in which the combined surgical and percutaneous technique offers a less invasive alternative to open surgery for the repair of aortic aneurysms or their main branches.||Clinical case: The case concerns a pre-term newborn of 30 weeks weighing 1,335 g. An umbilical catheter was introduced, which was withdrawn at 14 days due to an infection. It developed as Staphylococcus aureus with sepsis. The echocardiogram and Angio-CT confirmed AA, which were managed using a hybrid procedure of surgery and the endovascular implantation of 2 coated stents (Atrium V12 XR Medical Corp, Hudson, NH). The post-procedure clinical followups, including abdominal echo-tomography, confirmed the success of the treatment.||Conclusion: The endovascular aortic aneurysm repair procedure in premature newborns may be considered when deciding treatment of this disease, and could avoid the risks associated with open surgery.||However, follow-up and monitoring is required while the patient grows up, due to the possibility that the implanted stents require re-dilating. The outcomes of neonatal endovascular procedures in the future are unknown. (C) 2015 Sociedad Chilena de Pediatria. Published by Elsevier Espana, S.L.U.||UnlabelledAortic aneurysms (AA) in the paediatric population are uncommon. The use of umbilical catheters in neonates has been associated with infections and, on some occasions, the formation of aortic aneurysms. The surgical repair of these aneurysms is one type of treatment; however, percutaneous intervention with stents could provide an alternative treatment route, with fewer complications. The aim of this report is to present the therapeutic scope of a hybrid procedure, in which the combined surgical and percutaneous technique offers a less invasive alternative to open surgery for the repair of aortic aneurysms or their main branches.Clinical caseThe case concerns a pre-term newborn of 30 weeks weighing 1,335 g. An umbilical catheter was introduced, which was withdrawn at 14 days due to an infection. It developed as Staphylococcus aureus with sepsis. The echocardiogram and Angio-CT confirmed AA, which were managed using a hybrid procedure of surgery and the endovascular implantation of 2 coated stents (Atrium V12 XR Medical Corp, Hudson, NH). The post-procedure clinical follow-ups, including abdominal echo-tomography, confirmed the success of the treatment.ConclusionThe endovascular aortic aneurysm repair procedure in premature newborns may be considered when deciding treatment of this disease, and could avoid the risks associated with open surgery. However, follow-up and monitoring is required while the patient grows up, due to the possibility that the implanted stents require re-dilating. The outcomes of neonatal endovascular procedures in the future are unknown."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""5 páginas"", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC||ORCID"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1016/j.rchipe.2015.07.010"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""0370-4106"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:84946123701"", """", ""https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/209455||https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rchipe.2015.07.010"", """", ""WOS:000440793100010"", """", ""ESCUELA DE MEDICINA;LEMA FUXMAN GUILLERMO;S/I;99835||ESCUELA DE MEDICINA;SPRINGMULLER PINTO DANIEL;S/I;2187||ESCUELA DE MEDICINA;GONZALEZ FORETIC RODRIGO VICENTE;S/I;1006371||ESCUELA DE MEDICINA;GARAY GREVE FRANCISCO JAVIER;S/I;85500||Escuela de Medicina; Garay Greve, Francisco Javier; 0009-0003-9253-7082; 85500"", """", ""No. 5"", """", """", ""es"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""365"", """", ""361"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""REVISTA CHILENA DE PEDIATRIA-CHILE"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""03 Good health and well-being"", """", ""03 Salud y bienestar"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Tratamiento endovascular exitoso de aneurisma de aorta torácica secundario a infección de catéter de arteria umbilical en un recién nacido pretérmino||[Successful endovascular treatment of thoracic aortic aneurysm secondary to infection of the umbilical artery catheter in preterm infants]."", """", """", ""Successful endovascular treatment of thoracic aortic aneurysm secondary to infection of the umbilical artery catheter in preterm infants"", """", """", ""Tratamiento endovascular exitoso de aneurisma de aorta torácica secundario a infección de catéter de arteria umbilical en un recién nacido pretérmino||[Successful endovascular treatment of thoracic aortic aneurysm secondary to infection of the umbilical artery catheter in preterm infants]."", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Vol. 86"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""190162||99835||2187||152787||1006371||85500"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-05-24;190162;1||2021-05-24;99835;1||2021-05-24;2187;1||2021-05-24;152787;1||2021-05-24;1006371;1||2021-05-24;85500;1||2026-05-04;85500;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""b22ad03d-26aa-4ffe-9cd2-a29480d7b278"", """", """", ""Scopus||WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Converis;24-05-2021||Repositorio UC;08-07-2021||ORCID;2026-05-04"", """", """", ""Validado||Sin validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", ""Unpaywall"", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2021-05-24;190162;1||2021-05-24;99835;1||2021-05-24;2187;1||2021-05-24;152787;1||2021-05-24;1006371;1||2021-05-24;85500;1||2026-05-04;85500;1"", """"]","[""c20e36e8-788a-4d5a-8983-3a9fac973002"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""carga"", """", """", """", """", ""Borchert E||Lema G||Springmuller D||González K||Chang WT||González R||Garay F"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-05-04T12:54:19Z"", """", ""2026-05-04T12:54:19Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2015"", """", """", """", """", """", ""UnlabelledAortic aneurysms (AA) in the paediatric population are uncommon. The use of umbilical catheters in neonates has been associated with infections and, on some occasions, the formation of aortic aneurysms. The surgical repair of these aneurysms is one type of treatment; however, percutaneous intervention with stents could provide an alternative treatment route, with fewer complications. The aim of this report is to present the therapeutic scope of a hybrid procedure, in which the combined surgical and percutaneous technique offers a less invasive alternative to open surgery for the repair of aortic aneurysms or their main branches.Clinical caseThe case concerns a pre-term newborn of 30 weeks weighing 1,335 g. An umbilical catheter was introduced, which was withdrawn at 14 days due to an infection. It developed as Staphylococcus aureus with sepsis. The echocardiogram and Angio-CT confirmed AA, which were managed using a hybrid procedure of surgery and the endovascular implantation of 2 coated stents (Atrium V12 XR Medical Corp, Hudson, NH). The post-procedure clinical follow-ups, including abdominal echo-tomography, confirmed the success of the treatment.ConclusionThe endovascular aortic aneurysm repair procedure in premature newborns may be considered when deciding treatment of this disease, and could avoid the risks associated with open surgery. However, follow-up and monitoring is required while the patient grows up, due to the possibility that the implanted stents require re-dilating. The outcomes of neonatal endovascular procedures in the future are unknown."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""ORCID"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rchipe.2015.07.010||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/422111"", """", """", """", ""Escuela de Medicina; Garay Greve, Francisco Javier; 0009-0003-9253-7082; 85500"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""[S