5254b48b-07a0-44e0-acee-2822ad08f7a5,20876e81-99cb-40a1-bb84-c34c4e1e2c8c,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.issn,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""5254b48b-07a0-44e0-acee-2822ad08f7a5"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Hoke, Gd.||Latorre H., Claudio.||Guzmán R||Orszag Posa, Miguel, 1944-"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2017-04-11T20:50:59Z||2017-04-10T18:36:48Z"", """", ""2017-04-11T20:50:59Z||2017-04-10T18:36:48Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2009||2002"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Stable isotope altimetry is a useful tool for estimating paleoelevation in sedimentary records. Yet questions remain regarding how source moisture, climate, and local topography can influence these estimates. Here we present stable isotope altimetry results on late Quaternary pedogenic carbonates of known elevation on both flanks of the Andean orogen at 33 degrees S. We measured delta O-18 values of pedogenic carbonates and river water samples from small drainages at regular elevation increments within the Rio Aconcagua (Chile) and Rio Mendoza (Argentina) catchments. The delta O-18 values of river waters correlate well with elevation and show similar isotopic gradients between the Chilean (-3.7 parts per thousand/km) and Argentine (-4.8 parts per thousand/km) sides of the range. Uncertainties associated with scatter in the river water data and assumptions about the temperature of carbonate formation indicate that elevation estimates have 1 sigma errors of 350-450 m. We estimate the isotopic composition of soil water from pedogenic carbonates on both sides of the range by assuming mean annual temperatures based the modern temperature lapse rate from meteorological station data. Combined, our data show that stable isotope altimetry produces reasonable estimates of modern elevation, with the majority of our samples (60%) within the 1 sigma uncertainties and 77% within 2 sigma."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1130/G30308A.1"", """", """", """", ""1555-6611"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0091-7613"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:70450214724"", """", ""https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/279302||https://doi.org/10.1130/G30308A.1"", """", ""WOS:000271215600014"", """", ""FACULTAD DE CIENCIAS BIOLÓGICAS;LATORRE HIDALGO CLAUDIO;S/I;55090||INSTITUTO DE FÍSICA;ORSZAG POSA MIGUEL;S/I;98800"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Geology. Vol. 37, no. 11 (2009), p. [1015]-1018||Laser Physics. Vol. 12, no. 1 (2002), p. [77]-83"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Geology||Laser Physics"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""13 Climate action||06 Clean water and sanitation"", """", ""13 Acción por el clima||06 Agua limpia y saneamiento"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""The stable isotope altimeter: Do Quaternary pedogenic carbonates predict modern elevations?||The Stability of An Lon-Trap Laser"", """", """", """", """", """", ""The stable isotope altimeter: Do Quaternary pedogenic carbonates predict modern elevations?||The Stability of An Lon-Trap Laser"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""55090||98800"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-09-30;55090;1||2021-07-26;98800;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""41974||29583"", """", """", """", ""4f3c988e-cba1-4276-9c02-b5096c38c94f||4e75694d-44f0-41a4-af03-460d458706ca"", """", """", ""ISI-2006-2007-2008-2009-2012-2015||