28985e17-3eb4-43ab-a022-701b70c36bc8,cc2aa2a5-6f04-403d-8669-d43413d611fa,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""28985e17-3eb4-43ab-a022-701b70c36bc8"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Ashbaugh, Mark S.||Benguria Donoso, Rafael"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2017-04-10T20:44:23Z||2017-04-10T20:44:22Z"", """", ""2017-04-10T20:44:23Z||2017-04-10T20:44:22Z"", """", """", """", """", ""1993||2001"", """", """", """", """", """", ""We give several results which extend our recent proof of the Payne-Polya-Weinberger conjecture to ratios of higher eigenvalues. In particular we show that for a bounded domain Omega subset of R(n) the eigenvalues of its Dirichlet Laplacian obey lambda(4)/lambda(2)<j(n/2,1)(2)/j(n/2-1,1)(2) where lambda(m) denotes the mth eigenvalue and j(p,k) denotes the kth positive zero of the Bessel function J(p)(x). Certain extensions of this result are given, the most general being the bound lambda(kl(m))/lambda(m) less than or equal to sup lambda(k)/lambda(1) where k greater than or equal to 2 and l(m) denotes the number Omega'subset of R(n) of nodal domains of an mth eigenfunction. Our results imply certain further conjectures of Payne, Polya, and Weinberger concerning lambda(3)/lambda(2) and lambda(4)/lambda(3). In addition, we find a reasonably good bound on lambda(4)/lambda(1). We also briefly discuss extensions to Schrodinger operators and other elliptic eigenvalue problems."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1090/S0002-9947-00-02605-2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""0370-1646"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:23044523825"", """", ""https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/281097||https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-00-02605-2"", """", ""WOS:A1993MT55100002"", """", ""INSTITUTO DE FÍSICA;BENGURIA DONOSO RAFAEL JOSE URBANO;S/I;99598"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Proceedings of the Royal Society of Edinburgh. Vol. 123 A, no. 0 (1993), p. [977]-985||Transaction of the American Mathematical Society. Vol. 353, no. 3 (2001), p. [1055]-1087"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Proceedings of the Royal Society of Edinburgh||Transaction of the American Mathematical Society"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""510"", """", """", """", ""Matemáticas física y química"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Operador laplaciano||Ecuaciones diferenciales elípticas||Matemática||Matemáticas -Teoría espectral||Física Matemática"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Isoperimetric Bounds for Higher Eigenvalue Ratios for the N-Dimensional Fixed Membrane Problem||A Sharp Bound for the Ratio of the Firts Two Dirichlet Eigenvalues of a Domain in a Hemisphere of S-n"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Isoperimetric Bounds for Higher Eigenvalue Ratios for the N-Dimensional Fixed Membrane Problem||A Sharp Bound for the Ratio of the Firts Two Dirichlet Eigenvalues of a Domain in a Hemisphere of S-n"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""99598"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-09-30;99598;1||2021-07-26;99598;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""24103||28380"", """", """", """", ""6c6f4509-87ff-42cb-8427-e7eb30dff53a||d4ea34f1-7c75-459d-9df2-b315df0013e5"", """", """", ""Scopus||ISI-1991-1993-2003||WOS||ISI-2001-2011"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC;10-04-2017"", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", ""Unpaywall"", """", ""Val