dd5d4fb7-63df-49aa-92aa-258ec03dcb17,488dcadf-df43-4425-a599-2165ee6f4d2d,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""dd5d4fb7-63df-49aa-92aa-258ec03dcb17"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Paul D, Maria A.||Bravo, Alejandra, V||Beltran M, Constanza||Cerda L, Jaime||Angulo M, Daniela||Lizama C, Macarena||Alejandra Bravo V||Daniela Angulo M||Jaime Cerda L||Macarena Lizama C||María A. Paul D||Constanza Beltrán M"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-07-22T21:03:16Z||2021-09-20T17:12:25Z"", """", ""2021-07-22T21:03:16Z||2021-09-20T17:12:25Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2015"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Introduction: The children with Down syndrome (DS) are at increased risk of ear-nose-throat (ENT) disorders. International recommendations suggest early hearing screening and periodic specialist evaluation. Our goal was to characterize ENT disorders in children with DS, and propose recommendations for the Chilean population.||Patients and method: Cross-sectional, descriptive study, of children with DS, between 6 months and 15 years of age. The data was obtained by a health interview to the parents and review of medical records.||Results: We analyzed 134 patients with an average age of 44.5 months. The 78.8% had ENT disorders, the most frequent ENT disorders was allergic rhinitis and otitis media with effusion. Hearing screening was abnormal in a quarter of the patients, 50% of children over 3 years of age had obstructive sleep apnea diagnosed by polysomnogram. Older children had a statistically higher frequency of ENT disorders.||Conclusions: This series shows a high rate of ENT disorders in children with DS, which supports recommendations for hearing screening, high suspicion of obstructive sleep apnea and routine referral to an ENT specialist for prevention and aggressive therapy in order to reduce hearing loss and improve development of the child with DS. (C) 2015 Sociedad Chilena de Pediatria. Published by Elsevier Espana, S.L.U."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Unidad Académica"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""7"", """", """", """", ""WOS||Historial Académico"", """", """", """", ""María A. Paul D, Alejandra Bravo V, Constanza Beltrán M, Jaime Cerda L, Daniela Angulo M, Macarena Lizama C. Perfil de morbilidad otorrinolaringológica en niños con síndrome de Down. Revista Chilena De Pediatria. 2015;5(86):318-324."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1016/j.rchipe.2015.07.008"", """", """", """", ""0717-6228"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0370-4106"", """", """", """", ""MEDLINE:26342393"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:84946140788"", """", ""https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rchipe.2015.07.008||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/248388"", """", ""WOS:000440793100003"", """", ""Bachillerato; Paul Delfau, Maria De Los Angeles; 0000-0003-3995-3776; 3465||Escuela de Medicina; Cerda Lorca, Jaime Rodrigo; 0000-0003-3463-8304; 3935||Escuela de Medicina; Lizama Calvo, Macarena; 0000-0002-7116-8762; 10944||Medicina;Alejandra Bravo V;S/I;190157||Medicina;Daniela Angulo M;S/I;149117||Medicina;Jaime Cerda L;S/I;3935||Medicina;Macarena Lizama C;S/I;10944||Medicina;María A. Paul D;S/I;3465"", """", ""5||86"", """", """", ""es"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""324"", """", ""318"", """", """", """", """", """", ""SOC CHILENA PEDIATRIA"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""REVISTA CHILENA DE PEDIATRIA-CHILE||Revista Chilena de Pediatria"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""03 Good health and well-being"", """", ""03 Salud y bienestar"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Down syndrome||Trisomy 21||Obstructive sleep apnea syndrome||Hearing loss"", """", """", """", """", ""Ear, nose and throat disease