"en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""952"", """", ""950"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Blackwell Publishing Ltd"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Clinical and Experimental Dermatology"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Dermoscopy of blastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm in two patients"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Dermoscopy of blastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm in two patients"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""46"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""156251"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-04-29;156251;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS||Scopus||Pubmed"", """", ""Sin revisión"", """", """", """", ""Scopus;12-10-2021"", """", """", ""Sin Validar"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2025-04-29;156251;1"", """"]"
026bbcb2-b5f9-4798-b80d-42e155760e23,851a89b9-4895-41e2-9cb0-af1aebf37dd9,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.doi,dc.identifier.scopusid,dc.identifier.uri,dc.identifier.wosid",identifier_conflict,"[""026bbcb2-b5f9-4798-b80d-42e155760e23"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Alvares D.||Lázaro E.||Gómez-Rubio V.||Armero C.||Mattos T.B.||Matos L.A.||Lachos V.H.||Castro L.M."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-10-20T19:34:37Z||2022-07-29T16:23:52Z"", """", ""2021-10-20T19:34:37Z||2022-07-29T16:23:52Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2021||2022"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2021 John Wiley & Sons Ltd.Survival analysis is one of the most important fields of statistics in medicine and biological sciences. In addition, the computational advances in the last decades have favored the use of Bayesian methods in this context, providing a flexible and powerful alternative to the traditional frequentist approach. The objective of this article is to summarize some of the most popular Bayesian survival models, such as accelerated failure time, proportional hazards, mixture cure, competing risks, multi-state, frailty, and joint models of longitudinal and survival data. Moreover, an implementation of each presented model is provided using a BUGS syntax that can be run with JAGS from the R programming language. Reference to other Bayesian R-packages is also discussed.||© 2022 John Wiley & Sons Ltd.This article extends the semiparametric mixed model for longitudinal censored data with Gaussian errors by considering the Student's (Formula presented.) -distribution. This model allows us to consider a flexible, functional dependence of an outcome variable over the covariates using nonparametric regression. Moreover, the proposed model takes into account the correlation between observations by using random effects. Penalized likelihood equations are applied to derive the maximum likelihood estimates that appear to be robust against outlying observations with respect to the Mahalanobis distance. We estimate nonparametric functions using smoothing splines under an EM-type algorithm framework. Finally, the proposed approach's performance is evaluated through extensive simulation studies and an application to two datasets from acquired immunodeficiency syndrome clinical trials."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Ministerio de Ciencia e Innovaci?n||Fondo Nacional de Desarrollo Cient?fico y Tecnol?gico||FEDER||FAPESP‐Brazil||Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo||Coordenação de Aperfeiçoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior ‐ Brazil||Fondo Nacional de Desarrollo Científico y Tecnológico"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1002/sim.8933"", """", """", """", ""1097-0258"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0277-6715"", """", """", """", ""MEDLINE:33713474"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85102638896"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1002/(ISSN)1097-0258||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/332075||https://doi.org/10.1002/sim.8933"", """", ""WOS:000628336300001"", """", ""Facultad de Matemáticas; Alvares Da Silva, Danilo; 0000-0003-3764-0397; 1081962||Facultad de Matemáticas; Castro Cepero, Luis Mauricio; S/I; 151425"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""3020"", """", ""2975"", """", """", """", """", """", ""John Wiley and Sons Ltd"", """", """", """", """", ""Statistics in Medicine"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Statistics in Medicine"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto||acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""03 Good health and well-being"", """", ""03 Salud y bienestar"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Bayesian inference||JAGS||R-packages||time-to-event analysis||censored data||EM algorithm||HIV viral load||mixed-effects model||semiparametric model||Student's-t distribution"", """", """", """", """", ""Bayesian survival analysis with BUGS||Extending multivariate Student's-t semiparametric mixed models for longitudinal data with censored responses and heavy tails"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Bayesian survival analysis with BUGS||Extending multivariate Student's-t semiparametric mixed models for longitudinal data with censored responses and heavy tails"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""40"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""1081962||151425"", """", """", """", ""2023-01-05;1081962;1"", """", ""2023-01-05;1081962;1||2022-08-12;151425;0"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS||Scopus||Pubmed"", """", ""Sin revisión"", """", """", """", ""Scopus;12-10-2021||SCOPUS;2022-07-08"", """", """", ""Sin validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2023-01-05;1081962;1||2022-08-12;151425;1"", """"]","[""851a89b9-4895-41e2-9cb0-af1aebf37dd9"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Mattos T.B.||Matos L.A.||Lachos V.H.||Castro L.M."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2022-07-29T16:23:52Z"", """", ""2022-07-29T16:23:52Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2022"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2022 John Wiley & Sons Ltd.This article extends the semiparametric mixed model for longitudinal censored data with Gaussian errors by considering the Student's (Formula presented.) -distribution. This model allows us to consider a flexible, functional dependence of an outcome variable over the covariates using nonparametric regression. Moreover, the proposed model takes into account the correlation between observations by using random effects. Penalized likelihood equations are applied to derive the maximum likelihood estimates that appear to be robust against outlying observations with respect to the Mahalanobis distance. We estimate nonparametric functions using smoothing splines under an EM-type algorithm framework. Finally, the proposed approach's performance is evaluated through extensive simulation studies and an application to two datasets from acquired immunodeficiency syndrome clinical trials."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""FAPESP‐Brazil||Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo||Coordenação de Aperfeiçoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior ‐ Brazil||Fondo Nacional de Desarrollo Científico y Tecnológico"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1002/sim.9443"", """", """", """", ""1097-0258"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0277-6715"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85130250441"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1002/(ISSN)1097-0258||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/372383||https://doi.org/10.1002/sim.9443"", """", ""WOS:000799492100001"", """", ""Facultad de Matemáticas; Castro Cepero, Luis Mauricio; S/I; 151425"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""John Wiley and Sons Ltd"", """", """", """", """", ""Statistics in Medicine"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Statistics in Medicine"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""03 Good health and well-being"", """", ""03 Salud y bienestar"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""censored data||EM algorithm||HIV viral load||mixed-effects model||semiparametric model||Student's-t distribution"", """", """", """", """", ""Extending multivariate Student's-t semiparametric mixed models for longitudinal data wit