111a1e18-8e0c-49fe-a0cf-0f0f8df9dfed,0decdcfa-1741-40a8-adef-69f8aed8161c,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""111a1e18-8e0c-49fe-a0cf-0f0f8df9dfed"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Vicuña M.||De Cortillas C.T.||Magdalena Vicuña||Catalina Torres de Cortillas"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-10-20T19:35:16Z||2021-07-21T20:26:45Z"", """", ""2021-10-20T19:35:16Z||2021-07-21T20:26:45Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2021"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2021, Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Chile 1. All rights reserved.The COVID-19 pandemic transformed physical proximity into a possible threat and, with it, cast doubt on urban density as a value. But the opposite – the sprawled city – means longer commuting that punishes the lower classes. Hence, the question is not whether to densify or not but rather how to do it. This text addresses this question through the analysis of well-known recent cases from Santiago."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""National Research Center for Integrated Management of Natural Disasters||Conicyt||Fondecyt"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus||Historial Académico"", """", """", """", ""Magdalena Vicuña, Catalina Torres de Cortillas. Alta densidad en Santiago:Contribución de proyectos destacados al modelo de ciudad compacta. Arq (Santiago). 2021;(107):82-95."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.4067/S0717-69962021000100082"", """", """", """", ""0717-6996"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0716-0852"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85106181407"", """", ""http://www.scielo.cl/pdf/arq/n107/0717-6996-arq-107-82.pdf||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/332190||https://doi.org/10.4067/S0717-69962021000100082"", """", """", """", ""Instituto de Estudios Urbanos y Territoriales; Vicuna Del Rio, Maria M