were highly visited in summer and autumn, when avocados were not in bloom. NFS in orchards should be encouraged by policymakers because they support beneficial insects that could deliver ecosystem services and contribute to local biological conservation."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""ANID||Agencia Nacional de Investigación Científica y Tecnológica de Chile||Programa Regional de Investigación Científica y Tecnológica"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1111/afe.12447"", """", """", """", ""1461-9563"", """", """", """", """", """", ""1461-9555"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85105229955"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1111/(ISSN)1461-9563||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/332656||https://doi.org/10.1111/afe.12447"", """", ""WOS:000645853700001"", """", ""Facultad de Agronomía e Ingenieria Forestal; Zaviezo Palacios Tania; 0000-0002-4993-0386; 62543||Facultad de Agronomía e Ingenieria Forestal; Amouroux Paul Mathieu Edmond; S/I; 1015122||Facultad de Agronomía e Ingenieria Forestal; Munoz Gonzalez, Alejandra Ester; S/I; 11498"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Blackwell Publishing Ltd"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Agricultural and Forest Entomology"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""15 Life on land"", """", ""15 Vida de ecosistemas terrestres"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""floral traits||flower visitors||native bees||native flora||perennial flower strips"", """", """", """", """", ""Native flowering shrubs promote beneficial insects in avocado orchards"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Nati