"""", ""INSTITUTO DE ASTROFÍSICA;INFANTE LIRA LEOPOLDO;S/I;55248"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Astrophysical Journal. Vol. 596, no. 2 (2003), p. [143]-146"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Astrophysical Journal"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""520"", """", """", """", ""Astronomía"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Cúmulos de galaxias||Galaxias elípticas||Astronomía - Observaciones||Astronomía de rayos X"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Advanced Camera for Surveys Photometry of the Cluster Rdcs 1252.9-2927: the Color-Magnitude Relation At Z=1.24"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Advanced Camera for Surveys Photometry of the Cluster Rdcs 1252.9-2927: the Color-Magnitude Relation At Z=1.24"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""55248"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2022-01-05;55248;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""dd880585-fb77-4f51-bb05-ba27f365af66"", """", """", ""WOS||Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC;10-04-2017"", """", """", ""Validado"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2022-01-05;55248;1"", """"]"
d95f9e3c-e67e-409a-86a0-5a566e9db740,81e60530-efcc-4202-8a9b-7d9cdb81b83c,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.doi,dc.identifier.scopusid,dc.identifier.uri,dc.identifier.wosid",identifier_conflict,"[""d95f9e3c-e67e-409a-86a0-5a566e9db740"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Díaz M||Pérez P||Díaz Gutiérrez, Marco Aurelio"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-09-17T00:01:49Z||2022-01-03T18:55:27Z"", """", ""2021-09-17T00:01:49Z||2022-01-03T18:55:27Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2005"", """", """", """", """", """", ""We investigate the possibility of distinguishing between the standard model higgs boson and the lightest Higgs boson in split supersymmetry. We point out that the best way to distinguish between these two Higgs bosons is through the decay into two photons. It is shown that there are large differences of several per cent between the predictions for Gamma(h -> gamma gamma) in the two models, making possible the discrimination in future photon-photon colliders. Once the charginos are discovered in the next generation of collider experiments, the well-defined predictions for the Higgs decay into two photons will become a cross check to identify the light Higgs boson in split supersymmetry.||In the minimal supersymmetric standard model with bilinear R-parity violation, terms that violate R parity and lepton number are introduced in the superpotential inducing sneutrino vacuum expectation values. As a result, neutrino masses and mixing angles are generated via a low-energy seesaw mechanism. We show that this model embedded into an anomaly mediated supersymmetry breaking scenario is testable at a linear collider using charged Higgs boson production in association with a stau. This is possible in regions of parameter space where the charged Higgs boson and stau have similar mass, producing an enhancement of the charged scalar mixing angles. We show that the bilinear parameter and the sneutrino VEV can be determined from charged scalar observables, and estimate the precision of this determination."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""No tiene"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Historial Académico||Repositorio UC"", """", """", """", ""Díaz M, Pérez P. Can We Distinguish Between H(Sm) and H(0) in Split Supersymmetry?. Journal Of Physics G-Nuclear And Particle Physics. 2005;31(7):563-569."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1088/0954-3899/31/7/003"", """", """", """", ""1361-6471"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0954-3899"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:21244446690"", """", ""https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/287211||https://doi.org/10.1088/0954-3899/31/7/003"", """", ""WOS:000230868700004"", """", ""Física;Díaz M;S/I;104746||INSTITUTO DE FÍSICA;DIAZ GUTIERREZ MARCO AURELIO;S/I;104746"", """", ""7"", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""569"", """", ""563"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Journal of Physics G-Nuclear and Particle Physics. Vol. 31, no. 7 (2005), p. [563]-569"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Journal of Physics G-Nuclear and Particle Physics"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""510"", """", """", """", ""Matemáticas física y química"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Partículas elementales (Física)||Simetría (Física)||Teoría de campos (Física)"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Can We Distinguish Between H(Sm) and H(0) in Split Supersymmetry?"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Can We Distinguish Between H(Sm) and H(0) in Split Supersymmetry?"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""31"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""104746"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-09-16;104746;0||2022-01-05;104746;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""31671"", """", """", """", ""58b1a2a1-3992-4860-9289-4f23a8afc1d1"", """", """", ""ISI-2005-2006-2007-2008-2009-2010-2014||Scopus-2010-2014||WOS||Scopus"", """", ""Sin revisión"", """", """", """", ""Historial Académico;09-07-2021||Repositorio UC;10-04-2017"", """", """", ""Sin validar||Validado"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", ""Unpaywall"", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2021-09-16;104746;1||2022-01-05;104746;1"", """"]","[""81e60530-efcc-4202-8a9b-7d9cdb81b83c"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Díaz Gutiérrez, Marco Aurelio"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2022-01-03T18:55:27Z"", """", ""2022-01-03T18:55:27Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2005"", """", """", """", """", """", ""In the minimal supersymmetric standard model with bilinear R-parity violation, terms that violate R parity and lepton number are introduced in the superpotential inducing sneutrino vacuum expectation values. As a result, neutrino masses and mixing angles are generated via a low-energy seesaw mechanism. We show that this model embedded into an anomaly mediated supersymmetry breaking scenario is testable at a linear collider using charged Higgs boson production in association with a stau. This is possible in regions of parameter space where the charged Higgs boson and stau have similar mass, producing an enhancement of the charged scalar mixing angles. We show that the bilinear parameter and the sneutrino VEV can be determined from charged scalar observables, and estimate the precision of this determination."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1103/physrevd.67.115004"", """", """", """", ""1361-6471"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0954-3899"", """", """", """", """