"""", ""© 2023 The Authors. Magnetic Resonance in Medicine published by Wiley Periodicals LLC on behalf of International Society for Magnetic Resonance in Medicine.Purpose: QSM outside the brain has recently gained interest, particularly in the abdominal region. However, the absence of reliable ground truths makes difficult to assess reconstruction algorithms, whose quality is already compromised by additional signal contributions from fat, gases, and different kinds of motion. This work presents a realistic in silico phantom for the development, evaluation and comparison of abdominal QSM reconstruction algorithms. Methods: Synthetic susceptibility and (Formula presented.) maps were generated by segmenting and postprocessing the abdominal 3T MRI data from a healthy volunteer. Susceptibility and (Formula presented.) values in different tissues/organs were assigned according to literature and experimental values and were also provided with realistic textures. The signal was simulated using as input the synthetic QSM and (Formula presented.) maps and fat contributions. Three susceptibility scenarios and two acquisition protocols were simulated to compare different reconstruction algorithms. Results: QSM reconstructions show that the phantom allows to identify the main strengths and limitations of the acquisition approaches and reconstruction algorithms, such as in-phase acquisitions, water-fat separation methods, and QSM dipole inversion algorithms. Conclusion: The phantom showed its potential as a ground truth to evaluate and compare reconstruction pipelines and algorithms. The publicly available source code, designed in a modular framework, allows users to easily modify the susceptibility, (Formula presented.) and TEs, and thus creates different abdominal scenarios."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""ANID Fondecyt||Millennium Institute for Intelligent Healthcare Engineering CN2021_004||Cancer Research UK||Fondo Nacional de Desarrollo Científico y Tecnológico||Agencia Nacional de Investigación y Desarrollo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1002/mrm.29597"", """", """", """", ""1522-2594"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0740-3194"", """", """", """", ""36695213"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85147232079"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1002/(ISSN)1522-2594||https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.29597||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/376794"", """", ""WOS:000922334000001"", """", ""Escuela de Ingeniería; Tejos Nunez Cristian Andres; 0000-0002-8367-155X; 4027||Escuela de Medicina; Uribe Arancibia Sergio Andres; S/I; 16572||Escuela de Ingeniería; Arrieta Pellegrin Cristobal Ignacio; 0000-0001-8773-3722; 148591||Instituto de Ingeniería Biológica y Médica; Irarrazaval Mena Pablo; 0000-0002-5186-2642; 57376||Escuela de Ingeniería; Lambert Villanueva, Mathias Gabriel; S/I; 232597||Escuela de Medicina; Montalba Zalaquett, Cristian Andres; S/I; 1077325"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""John Wiley and Sons Inc"", """", """", """", """", ""Magnetic Resonance in Medicine"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Magnetic Resonance in Medicine"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""abdomen||digital phantom||liver QSM||MRI simulation||quantitative susceptibility mapping||water-fat separation"", """", """", """", """", ""Toward a realistic in silico abdominal phantom for QSM"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Toward a realistic in silico abdominal phantom for QSM"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""4027||16572||148591||57376|