1a9259f8-09a9-4825-876a-f353c349e015,fa360472-389d-41e3-b9ee-01ebad90e620,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""1a9259f8-09a9-4825-876a-f353c349e015"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""jwg||carga"", """", """", """", """", ""Ojeda Leal, Carolina||Quijada, Paula||Schroeder, Stella||Gutiérrez, Patricia||Bergamini, Kay||Leal C.O.||Quijada P.||Schroeder S.||Gutierrez P.||Bergamini K."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-11-03T16:28:21Z||2026-04-05T12:00:55Z"", """", ""2025-11-03T16:28:21Z||2026-04-05T12:00:55Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2026"", """", """", """", """", """", ""En Chile, el financiamiento nacional e internacional para iniciativas de restauración predial es una estrategia esencial para mitigar los efectos del cambio climático y prevenir incendios forestales. Este estudio etnográfico analiza un caso específico mediante observación no participante en reuniones comunitarias y visitas en terreno, lo que permitió evaluar las dinámicas y resultados de proyectos restauración post-incendios. Los hallazgos muestran que la corta duración de los proyectos (alrededor de 3 años) limitaría su impacto. Además, la falta de integración entre la restauración de especies nativas, y las acciones de prevención de incendios dificulta alcanzar el principal objetivo planteado que es el aumento de la captura de carbono. También, se observó una distribución desigual de beneficios que afectaría a personas que no tienen internet, que viven en lugares apartados y sin contactos que les incluyan en las postulaciones. A pesar de estas limitaciones, los liderazgos locales y equipos comprometidos han sido clave para sostener estas iniciativas.||© 2026 Revista de Geografia Norte Grande. All rights reserved.In Chile, the national and international funding for property restoration initiative is an essential strategy to mitigate the effects of climate change and prevent forest fires. This ethnographic study analyzes a specific case through on-participant observation in community meetings and field visits, which allowed evaluation of the dynamics and results of post-fire restoration projects. The findings show that the short duration of the projects (around 3 years) would limit their impact. In addition, the lack of integration between the restoration of native species and fire prevention actions makes it difficult to achieve the main objective which is to augment carbon sequestration. Also, an unequal distribution of benefits was observed that would affect people who do not have internet, who live in remote places and without contacts that include them in the applications. Despite the limitations, local leadership and committed teams have been key to sustaining these initiatives."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""ORCID||SCOPUS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.4067/S0718-34022026000100109"", """", """", """", ""0718-3402"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0379-8682"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105033280900"", """", ""https://doi.org/https://doi.org/10.4067/S0718-34022026000100109||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/413632"", """", """", """", ""Instituto de Estudios Urbanos y Territoriales; Ojeda Leal, Carolina Grace; 0000-0002-9830-9203; 1092333"", """", """", """", """", ""es||spa"", """", """", """", """", """", ""contenido completo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Revista de Geografia Norte Grande"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Revista De Geografía Norte Grande"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""300"", """", """", """", """", ""13 Climate action"", """", ""13 Acción por el clima"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Agentes transnacionales||Cambio climático||Gobernanza climática||Incendios forestales||Pequeños agricultores||Restauración predial||climate change||climate governance||forest fires||land restoration||small farmers||transnational agents"", """", """", """", """", ""Proyectos de Restauración Predial en Florida, Chile: Limitaciones y Oportunidades de Acción de Prevención de Incendios Promovidas desde Instituciones Públicas y Organismos Internacionales||Landowner Restoration Projects in Florida, Chile: Limitations and Opportunities for Wildfire Prevention Promoted by Public Institutions and International OrganizationsProyectos de Restauración Predial en Florida, Chile: Limitaciones y Oportunidades de Acción de Prevención de Incendios Promovidas desde Instituciones Públicas y Organismos Internacionales"", """", """", ""Landowner Restoration Projects in Florida, Chile: Limitations and Opportunities for Wildfire Prevention Promoted by Public Institutions and International Organizations"", """", """", ""Proyectos de Restauración Predial en Florida, Chile: Limitaciones y Oportunidades de Acción de Prevención de Incendios Promovidas desde Instituciones Públicas y Organismos Internacionales||Landowner Restoration Projects in Florida, Chile: Limitations and Opportunities for Wildfire Prevention Promoted by Public Institutions and International OrganizationsProyectos de Restauración Predial en Florida, Chile: Limitaciones y Oportunidades de Acción de Prevención de Incendios Promovidas desde Instituciones Públicas y Organismos Internacionales"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""1092333"", """", ""Validado"", """", """", """", ""3/25/2026"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-03-23;1092333;1||SCOPUS;2026-04-05"", """", """", ""Validado||Sin validar"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2025-10-30;1092333;1||2026-01-20;15065;1"", """"]","[""fa360472-389d-41e3-b9ee-01ebad90e620"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""carga"", """", """", """", """", ""Leal C.O.||Quijada P.||Schroeder S.||Gutierrez P.||Bergamini K."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-04-05T12:00:55Z"", """", ""2026-04-05T12:00:55Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2026"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2026 Revista de Geografia Norte Grande. All rights reserved.In Chile, the national and international funding for property restoration initiative is an essential strategy to mitigate the effects of climate change and prevent forest fires. This ethnographic study analyzes a specific case through on-participant observation in community meetings and field visits, which allowed evaluation of the dynamics and results of post-fire restoration projects. The findings show that the short duration of the projects (around 3 years) would limit their impact. In addition, the lack of integration between the restoration of native species and fire prevention actions makes it difficult to achieve the main objective which is to augment carbon sequestration. Also, an unequal distribution of benefits was observed that would affect people who do not have internet, who live in remote places and without contacts that include them in the applications. Despite the limitations, local leadership and committed teams have been key to sustaining these initiatives."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.4067/s0718-34022026000100109"", """", """", """", ""0718-3402"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0379-8682"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105033280900"", """", ""http://doi.org/10.4067/s0718-34022026000100109||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/421204"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""spa"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Revista de Geografia Norte Grande"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Revista de Geografia Norte Grande"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""climate change||climate governance||forest fires||land restoration||small farmers||transnational agents"", """", """", """", """", ""Landowner Restoration Projects in Florida, Chile: Limitations and Opportunities for Wildfire Prevention Promoted by Public Institutions and International OrganizationsProyectos de Restauración Predial en Florida, Chile: Limitaciones y Oportunidades de Acción de Prevención de Incendios Promovidas desde Instituciones Públicas y Organismos Internacionales"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Landowner Restoration Projects in Florida, Chile: Limitations and Opportunities for Wildfire Prevention Promoted by Public Institutions and International OrganizationsProyectos de Restauración Predial en Florida, Chile: Limitaciones y Oportunidades de Acción de Prevención de Incendios Promovidas desde Instituciones Públicas y Organismos Internacionales"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS;2026-04-05"", """", """", ""Sin validar"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", """", """"]"
77ebcebe-511a-4851-aed9-13e502eb58de,98ca9179-f0aa-4ab7-8971-e9b88b5715c5,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""77ebcebe-511a-4851-aed9-13e502eb58de"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""carga"", """", """", """", """", ""Gigoux J.P.||Contreras C.||Jofre P.||Claro J.C.||Juan Carlos Claro"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-03-22T14:33:59Z||2025-11-03T16:28:30Z"", """", ""2026-03-22T14:33:59Z||2025-11-03T16:28:30Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2025"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2025, Sociedad Medica de Santiago. All rights reserved.Graphic medicine is defined as the intersection between comics, Ilustration and the field of medicine. The concept was introduced by British physician Ian Williams in 2007 and has since evolved, offering a wide range of applications that have influenced both healthcare delivery and the education of health professionals. Today, this form of visual literature is experiencing a global rise, closely tied to the development of the medical humanities since the late 1990s. In particular, narrative medicine -the most recent branch of the medical humanities- has embraced graphic medicine as a powerful tool to better understand the human condition and patient subjectivity. Aim: To describe the current educational applications of graphic medicine in health professions training, and to highlight selected examples from Chile. Methods: A narrative review was conducted, focusing on literature and documented experiences regarding the use of graphic medicine in health education, with special attention to its implementation in Chile. Results: The review revealed a growing interest in the use of graphic medicine as an educational resource, emphasizing its potential to represent non-biomedical aspects of illness, such as emotional experiences, subjectivity, and social determinants of health. In Chile, several initiatives have employed graphic novels, comic strips, and visual narratives as pedagogical tools in the training of healthcare professionals, showing promising outcomes in fostering empathy, critical reflection, and a holistic understanding of patient care. Conclusions: The intentional use of graphic medicine in health education offers an effective approach to developing more well-rounded professionals-those who are not only scientifically competent but also skilled in humanistic dimensions of care. These visual tools serve as meaningful educational resources that support a more humanized, socially engaged, and ethically grounded approach to healthcare."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS||ORCID"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.4067/S0034-98872025000900640"", """", """", """", ""0717-6163"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0034-9887"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105017756973"", """", ""http://doi.org/10.4067/S0034-98872025000900640||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/420468"", """", """", """", ""Escuela de Medicina; Claro Garcia-Atance, Juan Carlos; S/I; 122201"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""640"", """", ""631"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Sociedad Medica de Santiago"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Revista Medica de Chile"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Education||Graphic Novels as Topic||Medical||Narrative Medicine"", """", """", """", """", ""Applications of Graphic Medicine in Health Professions EducationUtilidades de la medicina gráfica en la educación de profesiones sanitarias||Utilidades de la medicina gráfica en la educación de profesiones sanitarias"", """", """", ""