 negativelyassociated with eosinophilic esophagitis (OR: 0.11 [0.01–0.65], p = 0.042).Conclusions: In this study, H. pylori‐infected and uninfected children pre-sented similar frequencies of atopy. Further studies with larger cohorts areneeded to clarify the role of H. pylori in atopic conditions"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""ORCID"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1002/JPN3.70237"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""0277-2116"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105020599974"", """", ""https://doi.org/10.1002/JPN3.70237||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/414300"", """", """", """", ""Escuela de Medicina; Serrano Honeyman, Carolina Andrea; 0000-0001-5523-0637; 15296||Escuela de Medicina; Gil Galleguillos Pamela Yanet; S/I; 1046383||Escuela de Medicina; Castro Rodriguez Jose Antonio; 0000-0002-0708-4281; 113247"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Contenido parcial"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""610"", """", """", """", """", ""03 Good health and well-being"", """", ""03 Salud y bienestar"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Asthma||Eczema||Eosinophilic esophagitis||H. pylori infection||Rhinitis"", """", """", """", """", ""Lack of association between helicobacter pylori and pediatric atopy: evidence from a latin american multicenter cohort"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Lack of association between helicobacter pylori and pediatric atopy: evidence from a latin american multicenter cohort"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """"