9d2413e9-3687-4796-ae14-5171da176e69,aad90929-3e0b-4b68-a5e4-41b149297d2f,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""9d2413e9-3687-4796-ae14-5171da176e69"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""carga||vdr"", """", """", """", """", ""Palomera-Rojas P.||Arevalo A.M.||Rojas E.H.||Palomera Rojas, Pamela Verónica||Meneses Arévalo, Alejandra Cecilia||Hugo Rojas, Evelyn"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-03-22T14:41:34Z||2026-03-10T12:26:19Z"", """", ""2026-03-22T14:41:34Z||2026-03-10T12:26:19Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2025"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2025 Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Valparaiso. All rights reserved.The objective of this study was to identify how gender hierarchies are expressed in the conceptions of gender and science education, as well as in the declared teaching practices of the teachers’ educators (FdF). The research is conducted through a qualitative approach and in-depth case study design. The case studies involve four teacher educators who are recognized in the academic community for their sensitivity to gender in the science education field. Interviews were developed, which contemplated the use of a pedagogical dilemma. A dialogical discourse analysis (DDA) was performed. The results indicate that the FdF teachers position their conceptions from the visions of equity and plurality, which shows a reflective process about their teaching. This could have implications in the generation of educational practices that promote educational spaces that attend to diversity and inclusion.||El objetivo de este estudio fue caracterizar las jerarquías de género en las concepciones sobre el género y la educación científica, así como en las prácticas de enseñanza del profesorado Formador de Formadores (FdF). La investigación se lleva a cabo desde un enfoque cualitativo y se concreta en un estudio de casos en profundidad. Los casos de estudio consisten en cuatro FdF, reconocidos por la comunidad académica por ser sensibles a las temáticas de género en la educación científica. Se desarrollaron entrevistas, que contemplan el uso de un dilema pedagógico. Se realizó un análisis dialógico del discurso (ADD). Los resultados indican que el profesorado FdF posiciona sus concepciones desde las visiones de equidad y pluralidad, lo que da cuenta de un proceso reflexivo acerca de su enseñanza. Esto podría tener implicancias en la generación de prácticas educativas que promuevan espacios educativos que atiendan a la diversidad e inclusión."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""3/13/2026"", """", """", ""14 páginas"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS||ORCID"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.5027/psicoperspectivas-vol24-issue2-fulltext-3353"", """", """", """", ""0718-6924"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0717-7798"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105013111802"", """", ""http://doi.org/10.5027/psicoperspectivas-vol24-issue2-fulltext-3353||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/420516"", """", """", """", ""Facultad de Educación; Pamela Veronica Palomera Rojas; S/I; 1092077||Sede Regional de Villarrica; Meneses Arevalo, Alejandra Cecilia; 0000-0002-6563-5117; 16566||Facultad de Educación; Palomera Rojas, Pamela Verónica; S/I; 1092077||Facultad de Educación; Meneses Arévalo, Alejandra Cecilia; 0000-0002-6563-5117; 16566"", """", ""2"", """", """", ""spa||es"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Contenido completo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Valparaiso"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Psicoperspectivas"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""150"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""conceptions||gender||teacher educators||teaching practices"", """", """", """", """", ""Gender hierarchies in science education: conceptions and practices of teacher educatorsJerarquías de género en la educación científica: concepciones y prácticas del profesorado formador de formadores||Jerarquías de género en la educación científica: concepciones y prácticas del profesorado formador de formadores"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Gender hierarchies in science education: conceptions and practices of teacher educatorsJerarquías de género en la educación científica: concepciones y prácticas del profesorado formador de formadores||Jerarquías de género en la educación científica: concepciones y prácticas del profesorado formador de formadores"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""24"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""1092077||16566"", """", ""3/13/2026"", """", """", """", ""2026-07-19;1092077;1||2026-07-19;16566;1||2026-03-13;1092077;1||2026-03-13;16566;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS;2026-03-22||ORCID;2026-03-10"", """", """", ""Sin validar||Validado"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2026-07-19;1092077;1||2026-07-19;16566;1||2026-03-13;1092077;1||2026-03-13;16566;1"", """"]","[""aad90929-3e0b-4b68-a5e4-41b149297d2f"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""vdr"", """", """", """", """", ""Palomera Rojas, Pamela Verónica||Meneses Arévalo, Alejandra Cecilia||Hugo Rojas, Evelyn"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-03-10T12:26:19Z"", """", ""2026-03-10T12:26:19Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2025"", """", """", """", """", """", ""El objetivo de este estudio fue caracterizar las jerarquías de género en las concepciones sobre el género y la educación científica, así como en las prácticas de enseñanza del profesorado Formador de Formadores (FdF). La investigación se lleva a cabo desde un enfoque cualitativo y se concreta en un estudio de casos en profundidad. Los casos de estudio consisten en cuatro FdF, reconocidos por la comunidad académica por ser sensibles a las temáticas de género en la educación científica. Se desarrollaron entrevistas, que contemplan el uso de un dilema pedagógico. Se realizó un análisis dialógico del discurso (ADD). Los resultados indican que el profesorado FdF posiciona sus concepciones desde las visiones de equidad y pluralidad, lo que da cuenta de un proceso reflexivo acerca de su enseñanza. Esto podría tener implicancias en la generación de prácticas educativas que promuevan espacios educativos que atiendan a la diversidad e inclusión."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""3/13/2026"", """", """", ""14 páginas"", """", """", """", ""ORCID"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.5027/psicoperspectivas-Vol24-Issue2-fulltext-3353"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""https://doi.org/10.5027/psicoperspectivas-Vol24-Issue2-fulltext-3353||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/418564"", """", """", """", ""Facultad de Educación; Palomera Rojas, Pamela Verónica; S/I; 1092077||Facultad de Educación; Meneses Arévalo, Alejandra Cecilia; 0000-0002-6563-5117; 16566"", """", ""2"", """", """", ""es"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Contenido completo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Psicoperspectivas"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""150"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Jerarquías de género en la educación científica: concepciones y prácticas del profesorado formador de formadores"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Jerarquías de género en la educación científica: concepciones y prácticas del profesorado formador de formadores"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""24"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""1092077||16566"", """", ""3/13/2026"", """", """", """", ""2026-03-13;1092077;1||2026-03-13;16566;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""ORCID;2026-03-10"", """", """", ""Validado"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2026-03-13;1092077;1||2026-03-13;16566;1"", """"]"
f9b19511-78f8-46fa-b8b1-ca20097b1775,314afd58-c151-4958-9e41-4ebd2ae57253,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""f9b19511-78f8-46fa-b8b1-ca20097b1775"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""carga"", """", """", """", """", ""Herrera Styles Patricia Elen"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-07-20T12:00:09Z||2026-03-22T14:44:03Z"", """", ""2025-07-20T12:00:09Z||2026-03-22T14:44:03Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2025"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scientific racism, one of the most significant theories of thought of the 19th century, assumed the superiority of one of the human races: the white or Aryan, a hierarchy that had to be maintained in a biological sense for the protection of the species. In this scenario, the State would assume the role of protector of the integrity, superiority and purity of this race, acting through multiple fields and institutions. One of these areas was the fine arts, the Academy and the discipline of sculpture, which played a fundamental role due to their pregnancy and presence in public spaces. The present work investigates how this happened in Chile between 1854 and 1910, analyzing cases of local statuary that represent different races: Afros, indigenous people and whites, detailing the strategies that national sculptors used to aesthetically correct the bodies and demonstrate that the supposed The white race had a monopoly on beauty, intelligence and strength in an eminently mestizo country.||© 2025 Universidad de Talca. All rights reserved.Scientific racism, one of the most significant theories of thought of the 19th century, assumed the superiority of one of the human races: the white or Aryan, a hierarchy that had to be maintained in a biological sense for the protection of the species. In this scenario, the State would assume the role of protector of the integrity, superiority and purity of this race, acting through multiple fields and institutions. One of these areas was the fine arts, the Academy and the discipline of sculpture, which played a fundamental role due to their pregnancy and presence in public spaces. The present work investigates how this happened in Chile between 1854 and 1910, analyzing cases of local statuary that represent different races: Afros, indigenous people and whites, detailing the strategies that national sculptors used to aesthetically correct the bodies and demonstrate that the supposed The white race had a monopoly on beauty, intelligence and strength in an eminently mestizo country."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS||SCOPUS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.4067/S0718-23762025000100151"", """", """", """", ""0718-2376"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0716-498X"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105013368984"", """", ""https://doi.org/10.4067/S0718-23762025000100151||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/409078"", """", ""WOS:001527979400010"", """", ""Escuela de Psicología; Herrera Styles Patricia Elen; S/I; 84636||Escuela de Psicología; Herrera Styles Patricia Elen; 0000-0003-1206-0871; 84636"", """", ""1"", """", """", ""es||spa"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""173"", """", ""151"", """", """", """", """", """", ""UNIV TALCA, INST ESTUDIOS HUMANISTICOS JUAN IGNACIO MOLINA||Universidad de Talca"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""UNIVERSUM-REVISTA DE HUMANIDADES Y CIENCIAS SOCIALES||Universum"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""16 Peace, justice and strong institutions"", """", ""16 Paz, justicia e instituciones sólidas"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""sculpture||scientific racism||neoclassical academy||Foucault||Chile"", """", """", """", """", ""The Correction of Bodies: State Racism and Academic Sculpture in Chile (1854-1910)||The Correction of Bodies: State Racism and Academic Sculpture in Chile (1854-1910)A correção dos corpos: racismo de Estado e escultura acadêmica no Chile (1854-1910)LA CORRECCIÓN DE LOS CUERPOS: RACISMO ESTATAL Y ESCULTURA ACADÉMICA EN CHILE (1854-1910)"", """", """", """", """", """", ""The Correction of Bodies: State Racism and Academic Sculpture in Chile (1854-1910)||The Correction of Bodies: State Racism and Academic Sculpture in Chile (1854-1910)A correção dos corpos: racismo de Estado e escultura acadêmica no Chile (1854-1910)LA CORRECCIÓN DE LOS CUERPOS: RACISMO ESTATAL Y ESCULTURA ACADÉMICA EN CHILE (1854-1910)"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""40"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""84636"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-08-18;84636;1||2026-07-09;84636;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus||WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS;2025-07-19||SCOPUS;2026-03-22"", """", """", ""Sin validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", ""Unpaywall"", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2025-08-18;84636;1||2026-07-09;84636;1"", """"]","[""314afd58-c151-4958-9e41-4ebd2ae57253"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""carga"", """", """", """", """", ""Herrera Styles Patricia Elen"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-03-22T14:44:03Z"", """", ""2026-03-22T14:44:03Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2025"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2025 Universidad de Talca. All rights reserved.Scientific racism, one of the most significant theories of thought of the 19th century, assumed the superiority of one of the human races: the white or Aryan, a hierarchy that had to be maintained in a biological sense for the protection of the species. In this scenario, the State would assume the role of protector of the integrity, superiority and purity of this race, acting through multiple fields and institutions. One of these areas was the fine arts, the Academy and the discipline of sculpture, which played a fundamental role due to their pregnancy and presence in public spaces. The present work investigates how this happened in Chile between 1854 and 1910, analyzing cases of local statuary that represent different races: Afros, indigenous people and whites, detailing the strategies that national sculptors used to aesthetically correct the bodies and demonstrate that the supposed The white race had a monopoly on beauty, intelligence and strength in an eminently mestizo country."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.4067/s0718-23762025000100151"", """", """", """", ""0718-2376"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0716-498X"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105013368984"", """", ""http://doi.org/10.4067/s0718-23762025000100151||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/420529"", """", """", """", ""Escuela de Psicología; Herrera Styles Patricia Elen; 0000-0003-1206-0871; 84636"", """", """", """", """", ""spa"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""173"", """", ""151"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Universidad de Talca"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Universum"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Chile||Foucault||neoclassical academy||scientific racism||sculpture"", """", """", """", """", ""The Correction of Bodies: State Racism and Academic Sculpture in Chile (1854-1910)A correção dos corpos: racismo de Estado e escultura acadêmica no Chile (1854-1910)LA CORRECCIÓN DE LOS CUERPOS: RACISMO ESTATAL Y ESCULTURA ACADÉMICA EN CHILE (1854-1910)"", """", """", """", """", """", ""The Correction of Bodies: State Racism and Academic Sculpture in Chile (1854-1910)A correção dos corpos: racismo de Estado e escultura acadêmica no Chile (1854-1910)LA CORRECCIÓN DE LOS CUERPOS: RACISMO ESTATAL Y ESCULTURA ACADÉMICA EN CHILE (1854-1910)"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""40"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""84636"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-07-09;84636;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS;2026-03-22"", """", """", ""Sin validar"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2026-07-09;84636;1"", """"]"
698ea03a-11f2-4553-8604-8668d4e5c48a,8c0ab79d-8869-4940-bf35-7aee73ffd08e,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.doi,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""698ea03a-11f2-4553-8604-8668d4e5c48a"", ""123456789/2"", ""2574128"", """", """", """", ""carga||jca"", """", """", """", """", ""Barandiaran J.||Araya P.||Simonetti C.||Ragas J.||Barandiarán, Javiera||Araya, Paola||Simonetti Vicuña, Cristián Enrique||Ragas, José"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-03-22T14:52:35Z||2026-01-18T16:01:13Z"", """", ""2026-03-22T14:52:35Z||2026-01-18T16:01:13Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2025"", """", ""2026-01-18T16:01:16Z"", """", """", """", ""© 2025 The Author(s). Published by Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.Undone science refers to missing areas of scientific knowledge needed for decision-making or public policy. Though the term has become ubiquitous in STS research, it is hard to distinguish undone science from other possibilities like uncertainty, secrecy, or even unknowability. This paper advances a framework for distinguishing undone science from these other scenarios and applies it to the case of glacier management in Chile. Drawing on observations of glaciology science and regulatory documents, the authors compare how glacier science informed decisions on two Environmental Impact Assessments about new mines, nearly 20 years apart: Pascua Lama and Los Bronces, approved respectively in 2006 and 2023. The comparison shows a shift in Chilean glacier management, from a classic case of “undone science,” defined as that needed by specific mobilized or marginalized groups to advance their cause, to one of scientific controversy. In this second moment, contests over uncertainty or what counts as good or bad science dominate, creating a risk of leaving new areas of research undone. The analytical framework helps identify contests over scientific autonomy, validation, and pluralism and advances a clearer picture of how power is exercised, who holds it, and what science is (and is not) useful for.||Undone science refers to missing areas of scientific knowledge needed for decision-making or public policy. Though the term has become ubiquitous in STS research, it is hard to distinguish undone science from other possibilities like uncertainty, secrecy, or even unknowability. This paper advances a framework for distinguishing undone science from these other scenarios and applies it to the case of glacier management in Chile. Drawing on observations of glaciology science and regulatory documents, the authors compare how glacier science informed decisions on two Environmental Impact Assessments about new mines, nearly 20 years apart: Pascua Lama and Los Bronces, approved respectively in 2006 and 2023. The comparison shows a shift in Chilean glacier management, from a classic case of “undone science,” defined as that needed by specific mobilized or marginalized groups to advance their cause, to one of scientific controversy. In this second moment, contests over uncertainty or what counts as good or bad science dominate, creating a risk of leaving new areas of research undone. The analytical framework helps identify contests over scientific autonomy, validation, and pluralism and advances a clearer picture of how power is exercised, who holds it, and what science is (and is not) useful for."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""ANID||Fondecyt||Fondecyt"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""17 páginas"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS||SIPA"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1080/25729861.2025.2574128"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2572-9861"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105023493167"", """", ""http://doi.org/10.1080/25729861.2025.2574128||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/420631"", """", """", """", ""Escuela de Antropología; Simonetti Vicuna, Cristian Enrique; S/I; 119636||Instituto de Historia; Ragas Rojas, Jose Frank; S/I; 1081160||Instituto de Sociología; Simonetti Vicuña, Cristián Enrique; S/I; 119636"", """", ""1"", """", """", ""eng||en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""17"", """", ""1"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Routledge"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Tapuya: Latin American Science, Technology and Society"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Chile||climate change||Glaciers||scientific autonomy||undone science||Climate||Change"", """", """", """", """", ""Is glacier science undone, or just enough for a just transition? Reflections from Andean MinesA ciência dos glaciares é 'não feita', ou é apenas o suficiente para uma transição justa? Reflexões a partir das minas andinas¿Es la ciencia glaciar inconclusa o logra ser suficiente para avanzar una transición justa?: Reflexiones desde la minería de los Andes||Is glacier science undone, or just enough for a just transition? Reflections from Andean Mines"", """", """", ""A ciência dos glaciares é 'não feita', ou é apenas o suficiente para uma transição justa? Reflexões a partir das minas andinas||¿Es la ciencia glaciar inconclusa o logra ser suficiente para avanzar una transición justa?: Reflexiones desde la minería de los Andes"", """", """", ""Is glacier science undone, or just enough for a just transition? Reflections from Andean MinesA ciência dos glaciares é 'não feita', ou é apenas o suficiente para uma transição justa? Reflexões a partir das minas andinas¿Es la ciencia glaciar inconclusa o logra ser suficiente para avanzar una transición justa?: Reflexiones desde la minería de los Andes||Is glacier science undone, or just enough for a just transition? Reflections from Andean Mines"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """