a29324bb-d7c4-4bd9-90be-60f39e5f5487,a87af835-a584-4194-97af-93ad37991e24,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""a29324bb-d7c4-4bd9-90be-60f39e5f5487"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""CORREA, JA||FLORES, V||Correa M., Juan A."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-07-23T03:44:33Z||2017-04-11T14:43:00Z"", """", ""2021-07-23T03:44:33Z||2017-04-11T14:43:00Z"", """", """", """", """", ""1995"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Whitening of Gracilaria chilensis, accompanied by tissue softening and thallus fragmentation, was found to be associated with the presence of an endophytic amoeba. Although the symptoms developed originally in green mutant thalli, subsequent infections in the laboratory also affected normal, wild-type G. chilensis. Ultrastructural evidence indicates that the amoebae perforate the host cell walls of both cortical and medullary cells and digest their protoplasm. Feeding by the amoeba appears to involve both phagocytosis and enzymatic digestion of the host tissue. Destruction of the host tissue resulted in large cavities first, followed by thallus fragmentation. No other organism was found during the early stages of thallus invasion by the amoeba, although bacteria may appear once the amoeba reaches the inner tissues of the host."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""5"", """", """", """", ""WOS||Repositorio UC"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1007/BF00003800"", """", """", """", ""1573-5133"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0921-8971"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:0028894675"", """", ""https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00003800||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/259086"", """", ""WOS:A1995TA04900011"", """", ""Facultad de Ciencias Biológicas; Correa Maldonado, Juan Alberto; 0000-0002-0612-8780; 54626||FACULTAD DE CIENCIAS BIOLÓGICAS;CORREA MALDONADO JUAN ALBERTO;S/I;54626"", """", ""4"", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""425"", """", ""421"", """", """", """", """", """", ""KLUWER ACADEMIC PUBL"", """", """", ""Journal of Applied Phycology. Vol. 7, no. 4 (1995), p. [421]-425"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""JOURNAL OF APPLIED PHYCOLOGY"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""570"", """", """", """", ""Biología"", ""03 Good health and well-being"", """", ""03 Salud y bienestar"", """", """", """", ""Gracilaria - Investigaciones ||Alga roja||Botanica"", """", """", ""AMEBA||DECAY||FRAGMENTATION||GRACILARIA WHITENING||INFECTIOUS DISEASE||WHITE ROT"", """", """", """", """", ""WHITENING, THALLUS DECAY AND FRAGMENTATION IN GRACILARIA-CHILENSIS ASSOCIATED WITH AN ENDOPHYTIC AMEBA||Whitening, thallus decay and fragmentation in gracilaria Chilensis associated with an endophytic amoeba"", """", """", """", """", """", ""WHITENING, THALLUS DECAY AND FRAGMENTATION IN GRACILARIA-CHILENSIS ASSOCIATED WITH AN ENDOPHYTIC AMEBA||Whitening, thallus decay and fragmentation in gracilaria Chilensis associated with an endophytic amoeba"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""7"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""54626"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-09-11;54626;1||2021-09-30;54626;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""25427"", """", """", """", ""49efe584-1192-4958-b165-d930aa4d4403"", """", """", ""Scopus||WOS||ISI-1990-1993-1995-1996-1998-1999-2001-2002-2004-2005-2006-2011-2012-2013-2014-2015-2016||Scopus-2011-2012-2013-2015"", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS;05-06-2021||Repositorio UC;11-04-2017"", """", """", ""Sin validar||Validado"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", ""Unpaywall"", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2021-09-30;54626;1"", """"]","[""a87af835-a584-4194-97af-93a