655bd5f2-9950-44d9-a60d-d678b0a0c178,963bfce8-34e8-4ba9-b668-1e91ad0445b4,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.doi,dc.identifier.issn,dc.identifier.scopusid,dc.identifier.uri,dc.identifier.wosid",identifier_conflict,"[""655bd5f2-9950-44d9-a60d-d678b0a0c178"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Domínguez, C||Loewe Lobo, Marcelo Patricio, 1952-"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2017-04-10T18:36:23Z||2017-04-10T18:36:24Z"", """", ""2017-04-10T18:36:23Z||2017-04-10T18:36:24Z"", """", """", """", """", ""1995||2000"", """", """", """", """", """", ""A set of four finite energy QCD sum rules are used to determine the magnetic field dependence of the sum of the up- and down-quark masses of QCD, (m(u) + m(d)), the pion decay constant f(pi), the pion mass m(pi), the gluon condensate, <alpha(s)G(2)>, and the squared energy threshold for the onset of perturbative QCD, s(0), related to the Polyakov loop of lattice QCD. As a first input we take the magnetic evolution of the chiral quark condensate from lattice QCD and/or Nambu-Jona-Lasinio results. As a second input we take three different possible conditions concerning the quark and pion masses."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Repositorio UC"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1103/PhysRevD.98.034015"", """", """", """", ""1089-4918"", """", """", """", """", """", ""1550-7998"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85053007243"", """", ""https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/260300||https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.52.3143"", """", ""WOS:000441858000003"", """", ""INSTITUTO DE FÍSICA;LOEWE LOBO MARCELO PATRICIO ;S/I;55612"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Physical R