b838b275-8882-407a-9fbf-3efc3a2871e1,92e7015d-1374-4dd9-910b-9c63345c4397,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.doi,dc.identifier.pubmedid,dc.identifier.scopusid,dc.identifier.uri,dc.identifier.wosid",identifier_conflict,"[""b838b275-8882-407a-9fbf-3efc3a2871e1"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""grr"", """", """", """", """", ""Gonzalez Gallardo, Claudia Andrea||Garcia-huidobro Nuñez Francisco Gustavo||Lagos Villaseca, Antonia Elisa||Aliaga Durán, Rodrigo Francisco||Fuentes Lopez, Eduardo||Díaz, Luis Antonio||Garcia Salum, Tamara Cristal||Salinas Ortiz, Erick David||Toro, Adriana||Callejas, Claudio Andrés||Riquelme Perez, Arnoldo Javier||Medina, Rafael||Palmer, James||Yan C.H.||Tangbumrungtham N.||Maul X.A.||Ma Y.||Nayak J.V.||Hwang P.H.||Patel Z.M."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-10-20T19:31:11Z||2021-10-20T19:55:53Z"", """", ""2021-10-20T19:31:11Z||2021-10-20T19:55:53Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2021||2018"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2018 ARS-AAOA, LLCBackground: Acute exacerbations in patients with chronic rhinosinusitis (CRS) are often treated with courses of systemic antibiotics. Poor correlation between microbiologic culture results and the sinus microbiome in CRS has caused increased debate as to the relevance of culture-directed antibiotics. There is currently sparse data comparing outcomes of culture-directed antibiotics vs non-culture-directed antibiotics for treatment of CRS. Methods: This work reports a retrospective review. A total of 946 CRS patients treated with antibiotics were examined; 122 CRS patients with acute exacerbations were treated with culture-directed (n = 61) vs empiric (n = 61) antibiotics. Lund-Kennedy (LK) and 22-item Sino-Nasal Outcome Test (SNOT-22) scores were compared pretreatment and posttreatment, with short-term (<1 month) and long-term (1-6 months) follow-up. Patient demographics, comorbidities, and prior surgical history were collected. Results: Both groups had similar pretreatment SNOT-22 scores (p = 0.25) while the culture group had higher baseline LK endoscopy scores (p < 0.01). All data were adjusted for pertinent comorbidities, surgical history, co-therapeutics, and baseline scores. There was no difference in improvement in culture-directed and empirically treated groups in the short-term (p = 0.77) and long-term (p = 0.58) for minimal clinically important difference (MCID) of SNOT-22 and no difference in the short-term for LK scores (p = 0.11), but there was significantly more improvement in long-term LK scores in the culture-directed group (p = 0.01). Conclusion: Culture-directed therapy improves long-term endoscopy scores but does not yield an advantage in improving short-term endoscopy scores, nor in improving short-term and long-term quality of life scores in CRS patients. A prospective study is necessary to examine the relevance of routine microbiologic cultures in CRS patients."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""5 páginas"", """", """", """", ""ORCID||Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1002/alr.22798"", """", """", """", ""2042-6984"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2042-6976"", """", """", """", ""33848404"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85104228711"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1002/(ISSN)2042-6984||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/331785||https://doi.org/10.1002/alr.22798"", """", ""WOS:000639576300001"", """", ""Escuela de Medicina; Medina Silva Rafael Andres; 0000-0002-5013-6884; 1000649||Escuela de Medicina; Callejas Canepa Claudio Andres; S/I; 15885||Escuela de Medicina; Diaz Piga Luis Antonio; 0000-0002-8540-4930; 179253||Escuela de Medicina; Gonzalez Gallardo, Claudia Andrea; S/I; 8585||Escuela de Medicina; Garcia-huidobro Nuñez Francisco Gustavo; S/I; 1052053||Escuela de Medicina; Lagos Villaseca, Antonia Elisa; 0000-0002-2579-5474; 185024||Escuela de Medicina; Aliaga Durán, Rodrigo Francisco; S/I; 1072985||Escuela de Medicina; Fuentes Lopez, Eduardo; 0000-0002-0141-0226; 1013849||Escuela de Medicina; Garcia Salum, Tamara Cristal; 0000-0002-0170-9965; 121228||Escuela de Medicina; Salinas Ortiz, Erick David; S/I; 1101975||Escuela de Medicina; Riquelme Perez, Arnoldo Javier; 0000-0002-8259-8960; 3538||Escuela de Medicina; Maul Fonseca, Ximena; S/I; 156256"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", ""contenido parcial"", """", ""1277||1033"", """", ""1273||1028"", """", """", """", """", """", ""John Wiley and Sons Inc."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""International Forum of Allergy and Rhinology"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""610"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Anosmia||COVID-19||Dysgeusia||Hyposmia||Olfaction disorders||Risk for hospitalization||UPSIT||antibiotic||chronic rhinosinusitis||culture||exacerbation||infection||Lund-Kennedy||quality of life||SNOT-22||therapeutics"", """", """", """", """", ""Prospective assessment of smell and taste impairment in a South-American coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) cohort: Association with the need for hospitalization and reversibility of dysfunction||Comparison of outcomes following culture-directed vs non–culture-directed antibiotics in treatment of acute exacerbations of chronic rhinosinusitis"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Prospective assessment of smell and taste impairment in a South-American coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) cohort: Association with the need for hospitalization and reversibility of dysfunction||Comparison of outcomes following culture-directed vs non–culture-directed antibiotics in treatment of acute exacerbations of chronic rhinosinusitis"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""11||8"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""1000649||15885||179253||8585||1052053||185024||1072985||1013849||121228||1101975||3538||156256"", """", ""6/5/2024"", """", """", """", ""2025-04-29;1000649;1||2025-04-29;15885;1||2025-04-29;179253;1||2024-06-05;8585;1||2024-06-05;1052053;1||2024-06-05;185024;1||2024-06-05;1072985;1||2024-06-05;1013849;1||2024-06-05;121228;1||2024-06-05;1101975;1||2024-06-05;3538;1||2025-08-12;156256;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS||Scopus||Pubmed"", """", ""Sin revisión"", """", """", """", ""Scopus;12-10-2021"", """", """", ""Sin Validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2025-04-29;1000649;1||2025-04-29;15885;1||2025-04-29;179253;1||2024-06-05;8585;1||2024-06-05;1052053;1||2024-06-05;185024;1||2024-06-05;1072985;1||2024-06-05;1013849;1||2024-06-05;121228;1||2024-06-05;1101975;1||2024-06-05;3538;1"", """"]","[""92e7015d-1374-4dd9-910b-9c63345c4397"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Yan C.H.||Tangbumrungtham N.||Maul X.A.||Ma Y.||Nayak J.V.||Hwang P.H.||Patel Z.M."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-10-20T19:55:53Z"", """", ""2021-10-20T19:55:53Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2018"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2018 ARS-AAOA, LLCBackground: Acute exacerbations in patients with chronic rhinosinusitis (CRS) are often treated with courses of systemic antibiotics. Poor correlation between microbiologic culture results and the sinus microbiome in CRS has caused increased debate as to the relevance of culture-directed antibiotics. There is currently sparse data comparing outcomes of culture-directed antibiotics vs non-culture-directed antibiotics for treatment of CRS. Methods: This work reports a retrospective review. A total of 946 CRS patients treated with antibiotics were examined; 122 CRS patients with acute exacerbations were treated with culture-directed (n = 61) vs empiric (n = 61) antibiotics. Lund-Kennedy (LK) and 22-item Sino-Nasal Outcome Test (SNOT-22) scores were compared pretreatment and posttreatment, with short-term (<1 month) and long-term (1-6 months) follow-up. Patient demographics, comorbidities, and prior surgical history were collected. Results: Both groups had similar pretreatment SNOT-22 scores (p = 0.25) while the culture group had higher baseline LK endoscopy scores (p < 0.01). All data were adjusted for pertinent comorbidities, surgical history, co-therapeutics, and baseline scores. There was no difference in improvement in culture-directed and empirically treated groups in the short-term (p = 0.77) and long-term (p = 0.58) for minimal clinically important difference (MCID) of SNOT-22 and no difference in the short-term for LK scores (p = 0.11), but there was significantly more improvement in long-term LK scores in the culture-directed group (p = 0.01). Conclusion: Culture-directed therapy improves long-term endoscopy scores but does not yield an advantage in improving short-term endoscopy scores, nor in improving short-term and long-term quality of life scores in CRS patients. A prospective study is necessary to examine the relevance of routine microbiologic cultures in CRS patients."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1002/alr.22147"", """", """", """", ""2042-6984"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2042-6976"", """", """", """", ""29782068"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85047538017"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1002/(ISSN)2042-6984||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/334531||https://doi.org/10.1002/alr.22147"", """", ""WOS:000443132000008"", """", ""Escuela de Medicina; Maul Fonseca, Ximena; S/I; 156256"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""1033"", """", ""1028"", """", """", """", """", """", ""John Wiley and Sons Inc."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""International Forum of Allergy and Rhinology"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""antibiotic||chronic rhinosinusitis||culture||exacerbation||infection||Lund-Kennedy||quality of life||SNOT-22||therapeutics"", """", """", """", """", ""Comparison of outcomes following culture-directed vs non–culture-directed antibiotics in treatment of acute exacerbations of chronic rhinosinusitis"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Comparison of outcomes following culture-directed vs non–culture-directed antibiotics in treatment of acute exacerbations of chronic rhinosinusitis"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""8"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""156256"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-08-12;156256;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS||Scopus||Pubmed"", """", ""Sin revisión"", """", """", """", ""Scopus;12-10-2021"", """", """", ""Sin validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", """", """"]"
6d61027f-be63-4b99-81e4-a4629c0c342d,ea17e176-6535-4c2e-ab6a-4dfe12245d3e,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.doi,dc.identifier.scopusid,dc.identifier.uri,dc.identifier.wosid",identifier_conflict,"[""6d61027f-be63-4b99-81e4-a4629c0c342d"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""López-Llunell C.||Romaní J.||Roé E.||Giavedoni P.||Vidal D.||Wortsman X.||Moll-Manzur C.||Ramírez-Cornejo C.||Vera-Kellet C.||Alfaro-Sepúlveda D.||Mellado-Francisco G.||Rezende J."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-10-20T19:38:05Z||2021-10-20T19:38:07Z"", """", ""2021-10-20T19:38:05Z||2021-10-20T19:38:07Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2021"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2021 American Institute of Ultrasound in MedicineSarcoidosis is a multiorgan disease characterized by the formation of noncaseating granulomas and possible skin involvement. Cutaneous sarcoidosis (CS) can be explored by ultrasonography when deep dermal or subcutaneous nodules are the clinical presentation. We reviewed the ultrasound characteristics of 14 patients (86% female; mean age, 55 years) with CS. Ultrasonography revealed dermal or subcutaneous hypoechoic areas with increased echogenicity and hypervascularity of the neighboring subcutaneous tissue. In 42.9% of cases a cobblestone pattern of the subcutaneous tissue suggestive of septal involvement was detected. These US features can support the detection of dermal and subcutaneous abnormalities in CS and its early diagnosis.||© 2021 American Institute of Ultrasound in MedicineObjectives: To detect ultrasonographic inflammatory signs in the lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular glands in cosmetic fillers (CFs) users. Methods: A prospective and cross-sectional ultrasound study of the glands in cases with CFs was performed. The sample included users of hyaluronic acid, silicone oil, polymethylmethacrylate, polycaprolactone, calcium hydroxyapatite, and polyacrylamide. Abnormalities of the parenchyma and hypervascularity signs of the glands were compared with a control group (n = 10), evaluated by 2 observers, and correlated with the type, number, and location of the facial CFs. Cohen's kappa test and logistic regression models with odds ratios (OR) adjusted by age with 95% CI were performed. Results: Sixty-three patients with CFs met the criteria. Parotid and submandibular glands had the highest percentage of parenchymal involvement: 87.3 and 88.9%, respectively (p <.01). Abnormalities of the echostructure of the parenchyma and hypervascularity of the glands were detected with all kinds of fillers without significant differences per type. A significant substantial interrater kappa (0.61) with an agreement of 90% for all glands among observers was found. Conclusion: Users of common types of CFs frequently present subclinical ultrasonographic signs of inflammation of the lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular glands. Further research on the topic seems necessary."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1002/jum.15631"", """", """", """", ""1550-9613"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0278-4297"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85099424477"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1002/(ISSN)1550-9613||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/332767||https://doi.org/10.1002/jum.15631"", """", ""WOS:000608452600001"", """", ""Escuela de Medicina||Escuela de Medicina; Vera Kellet Cristian Andres; 0000-0001-8697-9245; 9379||Escuela de Medicina; Wortsman Canovas Ximena Loreto; 0000-0003-3359-5023; 1043349"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""John Wiley and Sons Ltd"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Journal of Ultrasound in Medicine"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""03 Good health and well-being"", """", ""03 Salud y bienestar"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""cutaneous sarcoidosis||dermatologic ultrasound||sarcoidosis||sarcoidosis ultrasound||cosmetic fillers ultrasound||fillers ultrasound||lacrimal gland ultrasound||parotid gland ultrasound||salivary glands ultrasound||submandibular gland ultrasound||ultrasound"", """", """", """", """", ""Ultrasonographic patterns of cutaneous sarcoidosis||Ultrasonographic subclinical signs of inflammation of the lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular glands in users of cosmetic fillers"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Ultrasonographic patterns of cutaneous sarcoidosis||Ultrasonographic subclinical signs of inflammation of the lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular glands in users of cosmetic fillers"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""1043349||9379"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-07-22;1043349;1||2025-04-29;9379;1||2025-04-29;1043349;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus||WOS"", """", ""Sin revisión"", """", """", """", ""Scopus;12-10-2021"", """", """", ""Sin validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2025-04-29;9379;1||2025-04-29;1043349;1"", """"]","[""ea17e176-6535-4c2e-ab6a-4dfe12245d3e"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Wortsman X.||Moll-Manzur C.||Ramírez-Cornejo C.||Vera-Kellet C.||Alfaro-Sepúlveda D.||Mellado-Francisco G.||Rezende J."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-10-20T19:38:07Z"", """", ""2021-10-20T19:38:07Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2021"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2021 American Institute of Ultrasound in MedicineObjectives: To detect ultrasonographic inflammatory signs in the lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular glands in cosmetic fillers (CFs) users. Methods: A prospective and cross-sectional ultrasound study of the glands in cases with CFs was performed. The sample included users of hyaluronic acid, silicone oil, polymethylmethacrylate, polycaprolactone, calcium hydroxyapatite, and polyacrylamide. Abnormalities of the parenchyma and hypervascularity signs of the glands were compared with a control group (n = 10), evaluated by 2 observers, and correlated with the type, number, and location of the facial CFs. Cohen's kappa test and logistic regression models with odds ratios (OR) adjusted by age with 95% CI were performed. Results: Sixty-three patients with CFs met the criteria. Parotid and submandibular glands had the highest percentage of parenchymal involvement: 87.3 and 88.9%, respectively (p <.01). Abnormalities of the echostructure of the parenchyma and hypervascularity of the glands were detected with all kinds of fillers without significant differences per type. A significant substantial interrater kappa (0.61) with an agreement of 90% for all glands among observers was found. Conclusion: Users of common types of CFs frequently present subclinical ultrasonographic signs of inflammation of the lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular glands. Further research on the topic seems necessary."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1002/jum.15621"", """", """", """", ""1550-9613"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0278-4297"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85099083466"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1002/(ISSN)1550-9613||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/332779||https://doi.org/10.1002/jum.15621"", """", ""WOS:000605752000001"", """", ""Escuela de Medicina; Vera Kellet Cristian Andres; 0000-0001-8697-9245; 9379||Escuela de Medicina; Wortsman Canovas Ximena Loreto; 0000-0003-3359-5023; 1043349"", """", """", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""John Wiley and Sons Ltd"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Journal of Ultrasound in Medicine"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""cosmetic fillers ultrasound||dermatologic ultrasound||fillers ultrasound||lacrimal gland ultrasound||parotid gland ultrasound||salivary glands ultrasound||submandibular gland ultrasound||ultrasound"", """", """", """", """", ""Ultrasonographic subclinical signs of inflammation of the lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular glands in users of cosmetic fillers"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Ultrasonographic subclinical signs of inflammation of the lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular glands in users of cosmetic fillers"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""9379||1043349"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-04-29;9379;1||2025-04-29;1043349;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus||WOS"", """", ""Sin revisión"", """", """", """", ""Scopus;12-10-2021"", """", """", ""Sin Validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2025-04-29;9379;1||2025-04-29;1043349;1"", """"]"
1aa93d55-e9fc-4a84-8a9a-1e397292bfda,fe0eeec1-a7e1-4303-a0fd-b0d72fdf9072,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.doi,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""1aa93d55-e9fc-4a84-8a9a-1e397292bfda"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""aba"", """", """", """", """", ""Parra Carrasco, Fredy Omar||Parra, Fredy"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-01-02T22:16:02Z||2025-03-02T11:03:26Z"", """", ""2025-01-02T22:16:02Z||2025-03-02T11:03:26Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2024"", """", ""2025-01-02T22:16:05Z"", """", """", """", ""El presente artículo se pregunta principalmente por la visión del mal y la crisis definitiva de la teodicea en el pensamiento del filósofo judío Emmanuel Levinas (1906-1995). Revisando sus ensayos más sistemáticos sobre el asunto se destacan las nociones del mal como exceso, como horror y sufrimiento inútil. Para contextualizar la cuestión central se aborda la emergencia del mal absoluto y la experiencia del horror de Auschwitz en el testimonio de víctimas sobrevivientes y en la reflexión filosófica y religiosa de algunas voces de la filosofía judía contemporánea.||The present article is mainly concerned with the vision of evil and the ultimate cri-sis of theodicy in the thought of the Jewish philosopher Emmanuel Levinas (1906-1995). In this article, I review Levinas’s most systematic essays on the subject, em-phasizing the notions of evil as excess, horror, and useless suffering. In order to contextualize the central question, I point out the emergence of absolute evil and he experience of the horror of Auschwitz in the testimony of surviving victims and the philosophical and religious reflection of some voices of contemporary Jew-ish philosophy.||The present article is mainly concerned with the vision of evil and the ultimate crisis of theodicy in the thought of the Jewish philosopher Emmanuel Levinas (19061995). In this article, I review Levinas's most systematic essays on the subject, emphasizing the notions of evil as excess, horror, and useless suffering. In order to contextualize the central question, I point out the emergence of absolute evil and the experience of the horror of Auschwitz in the testimony of surviving victims and the philosophical and religious reflection of some voices of contemporary Jewish philosophy."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""1/14/2025"", """", """", ""28 páginas"", """", """", """", ""SIPA||WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""9866596"", """", ""10.46553/teo.61.145.2024.p.167-194"", """", """", """", ""2683-7307"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0328-1396"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""https://doi.org/10.46553/teo.61.145.2024.p167-194||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/402563"", """", ""WOS:001417799400007"", """", ""Facultad de Teología; Parra Carrasco, Fredy Omar; 0000-0002-1217-5612; 70417"", """", ""145"", """", """", ""es||en"", """", """", """", """", """", ""contenido completo"", """", ""194"", """", ""167"", """", """", """", """", """", ""PONTIFICIA UNIV CATOLICA ARGENTINA, FAC TEOLOGIA"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Revista Teología||TEOLOGIA"", """", """", """", ""Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International"", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", ""https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""100|"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Mal||Teodicea||Auschwitz||Sufrimiento inútil||Responsabilidad||Memoria||Emmanuel Levinas||Evil||Theodicy||Useless Suffering||Responsibility||Memory||philosophy. Evil"", """", """", """", """", ""El mal en el pensamiento de Emmanuel Levinas||Evil in the thought of Emmanuel Levinas"", """", """", ""Evil in the thought of Emmanuel Levinas"", """", """", ""El mal en el pensamiento de Emmanuel Levinas||Evil in the thought of Emmanuel Levinas"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""LXI||61"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""70417"", """", ""1/14/2025"", """", """", """", ""2025-01-14;70417;1||2025-07-21;70417;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Dialnet||Erihplus||WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS;2025-03-01"", """", """", ""Validado||Sin validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", ""Unpaywall"", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2025-01-14;70417;1"", """"]","[""fe0eeec1-a7e1-4303-a0fd-b0d72fdf9072"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Parra, Fredy"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-03-02T11:03:26Z"", """", ""2025-03-02T11:03:26Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2024"", """", """", """", """", """", ""The present article is mainly concerned with the vision of evil and the ultimate crisis of theodicy in the thought of the Jewish philosopher Emmanuel Levinas (19061995). In this article, I review Levinas's most systematic essays on the subject, emphasizing the notions of evil as excess, horror, and useless suffering. In order to contextualize the central question, I point out the emergence of absolute evil and the experience of the horror of Auschwitz in the testimony of surviving victims and the philosophical and religious reflection of some voices of contemporary Jewish philosophy."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.46553/teo.61.145.2024.p167-194"", """", """", """", ""2683-7307"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0328-1396"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""https://doi.org/10.46553/teo.61.145.2024.p167-194||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/403686"", """", ""WOS:001417799400007"", """", ""Facultad de Teología; Parra Carrasco, Fredy Omar; 0000-0002-1217-5612; 70417"", """", ""145"", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""PONTIFICIA UNIV CATOLICA ARGENTINA, FAC TEOLOGIA"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""TEOLOGIA"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""philosophy. Evil||Theodicy||Auschwitz||Useless Suffering||Responsibility||Memory||Emmanuel Levinas"", """", """", """", """", ""Evil in the thought of Emmanuel Levinas"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Evil in the thought of Emmanuel Levinas"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""61"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""70417"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-07-21;70417;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS;2025-03-01"", """", """", ""Sin validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", ""Unpaywall"", """", ""Validado"", """", """", """"]"
edf03c31-9c66-48a5-a851-41d6ba640bba,e54239ec-644e-4fce-b796-6774fd392af7,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.doi,dc.identifier.pubmedid,dc.identifier.scopusid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""edf03c31-9c66-48a5-a851-41d6ba640bba"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Olszewski P.K.||Noble E.E.||Paiva L.||Ueta Y.||Blevins J.||Ávalos Y.||Kerr B.||Maliqueo M.||Dorfman M."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2022-03-30T20:46:57Z||2021-10-20T19:55:14Z"", """", ""2022-03-30T20:46:57Z||2021-10-20T19:55:14Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2022||2018"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2022 British Society for Neuroendocrinology. This article has been contributed to by U.S. Government employees and their work is in the public domain in the USA.The neuropeptide oxytocin (OT) has emerged as an important anorexigen in the regulation of food intake and energy balance. It has been shown that the release of OT and activation of hypothalamic OT neurons coincide with food ingestion. Its effects on feeding have largely been attributed to limiting meal size through interactions in key regulatory brain regions governing the homeostatic control of food intake such as the hypothalamus and hindbrain in addition to key feeding reward areas such as the nucleus accumbens and ventral tegmental area. Furthermore, the magnitude of an anorexigenic response to OT and feeding-related activation of the brain OT circuit are modified by the composition and flavor of a diet, as well as by a social context in which a meal is consumed. OT is particularly effective in reducing consumption of carbohydrates and sweet tastants. Pharmacologic, genetic, and pair-feeding studies indicate that OT-elicited weight loss cannot be fully explained by reductions of food intake and that the overall impact of OT on energy balance is also partly a result of OT-elicited changes in lipolysis, energy expenditure, and glucose regulation. Peripheral administration of OT mimics many of its effects when it is given into the central nervous system, raising the questions of whether and to what extent circulating OT acts through peripheral OT receptors to regulate energy balance. Although OT has been found to elicit weight loss in female mice, recent studies have indicated that sex and estrous cycle may impact oxytocinergic modulation of food intake. Despite the overall promising basic research data, attempts to use OT in the clinical setting to combat obesity and overeating have generated somewhat mixed results. The focus of this mini-review is to briefly summarize the role of OT in feeding and metabolism, address gaps and inconsistencies in our knowledge, and discuss some of the limitations to the potential use of chronic OT that should help guide future research on OT as a tailor-made anti-obesity therapeutic.||© 2018 British Society for NeuroendocrinologyDiet-induced obesity (DIO) is associated with chronic, low-grade inflammation in the hypothalamus, a key regulator of energy homeostasis. Current studies have revealed the involvement of different cell types, as well as cell and molecular mechanisms, that contribute to diet-induced hypothalamic inflammation (DIHI) and DIO. Subsequent to the discovery that high-fat diet and saturated fatty acids increase the expression of hypothalamic cytokines prior to weight gain, research has focused on understanding the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying these changes, in addition to the role of inflammation in the pathogenesis of obesity. Recent studies have proposed that the inhibition of pro-inflammatory pathways in microglia and astrocytes is sufficient to protect against DIHI and prevent obesity. In addition, impairment of intracellular and epigenetic mechanisms, such as hypothalamic autophagy and changes in the methylation pattern of certain genes, have been implicated in susceptibility to DIHI and DIO. Interestingly, a sexual dimorphism has been found during DIO in hypothalamic inflammation, glial activation and metabolic diseases, and recent data support an important role of sex steroids in DIHI. These new exciting findings uncover novel obesity pathogenic mechanisms and provide targets to develop therapeutic approaches."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""ANID FONDECYT||Agencia Nacional de Investigación y Desarrollo||Department of Veterans Affairs Biomedical Laboratory Research and Development Service||Medical Research Service||Royal Society of New Zealand Marsden||National Institutes of Health||Department of Veterans Affairs||Office of Research and Development||American Heart Association||University of Washington||Diabetes Research Center||Nutrition Obesity Research Center||Comisión Nacional de Investigación Científica y Tecnológica||Fondo Nacional de Desarrollo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1111/jne.13106"", """", """", """", ""1365-2826"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0953-8194"", """", """", """", ""35192207"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85125055825"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1111/(ISSN)1365-2826||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/367726||https://doi.org/10.1111/jne.13106"", """", ""WOS:000446990900001"", """", ""Interdisciplinarias; Paiva Maldonado, Luis Alberto; S/I; 1248188"", """", ""e12598"", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""John Wiley and Sons Inc||Blackwell Publishing Ltd"", """", """", """", """", ""Journal of Neuroendocrinology"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Journal of Neuroendocrinology"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""03 Good health and well-being"", """", ""03 Salud y bienestar"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""energy expenditure||food intake||meal size||obesity||oxytocin||autophagy||diet-induced obesity||epigenetics||high-fat diet||sex steroids"", """", """", """", """", ""Oxytocin as a potential pharmacological tool to combat obesity||Cell and molecular mechanisms behind diet-induced hypothalamic inflammation and obesity"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Oxytocin as a potential pharmacological tool to combat obesity||Cell and molecular mechanisms behind diet-induced hypothalamic inflammation and obesity"", ""reseña||artículo de revisión"", """", """", """", """", """", ""30"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Si"", """", """", ""1248188"", """", """", """", """", """", ""2023-12-02;1248188;0"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus||WOS||Pubmed"", """", ""Sin revisión"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS;21-03-2022||Scopus;12-10-2021"", """", """", ""Sin validar"", """", ""OSDG;2025-12-22"", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2023-12-02;1248188;1"", """"]","[""e54239ec-644e-4fce-b796-6774fd392af7"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Ávalos Y.||Kerr B.||Maliqueo M.||Dorfman M."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2021-10-20T19:55:14Z"", """", ""2021-10-20T19:55:14Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2018"", """", """", """", """", """", ""© 2018 British Society for NeuroendocrinologyDiet-induced obesity (DIO) is associated with chronic, low-grade inflammation in the hypothalamus, a key regulator of energy homeostasis. Current studies have revealed the involvement of different cell types, as well as cell and molecular mechanisms, that contribute to diet-induced hypothalamic inflammation (DIHI) and DIO. Subsequent to the discovery that high-fat diet and saturated fatty acids increase the expression of hypothalamic cytokines prior to weight gain, research has focused on understanding the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying these changes, in addition to the role of inflammation in the pathogenesis of obesity. Recent studies have proposed that the inhibition of pro-inflammatory pathways in microglia and astrocytes is sufficient to protect against DIHI and prevent obesity. In addition, impairment of intracellular and epigenetic mechanisms, such as hypothalamic autophagy and changes in the methylation pattern of certain genes, have been implicated in susceptibility to DIHI and DIO. Interestingly, a sexual dimorphism has been found during DIO in hypothalamic inflammation, glial activation and metabolic diseases, and recent data support an important role of sex steroids in DIHI. These new exciting findings uncover novel obesity pathogenic mechanisms and provide targets to develop therapeutic approaches."", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""American Heart Association||University of Washington||Diabetes Research Center||Nutrition Obesity Research Center||Nutrition Obesity Research Center||Comisión Nacional de Investigación Científica y Tecnológica||Fondo Nacional de Desarrollo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.1111/jne.12598"", """", """", """", ""1365-2826"", """", """", """", """", """", ""0953-8194"", """", """", """", ""29645315"", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:85052491612"", """", ""http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/10.1111/(ISSN)1365-2826||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/334494||https://doi.org/10.1111/jne.12598"", """", ""WOS:000446990900001"", """", """", """", ""e12598"", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Blackwell Publishing Ltd"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Journal of Neuroendocrinology"", """", """", """", """", """", ""acceso restringido"", """", """", """", 