9503e87c-4e85-4a85-bdcf-262446cf0ed2,de19f93c-2a44-4450-87b3-77fe39a44aff,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""9503e87c-4e85-4a85-bdcf-262446cf0ed2"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""carga"", """", """", """", """", ""Rodriguez-Leiva, Sebastian||Rodriguez, Norma Angelica||Hidalgo, Rodrigo||Vieyra, Antonio||Montes, Octavio"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-03-21T16:05:20Z||2025-12-16T00:25:34Z"", """", ""2026-03-21T16:05:20Z||2025-12-16T00:25:34Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2025"", """", """", """", """", """", ""The increase in avocado consumption has led to an expansion of monoculture areas and the exacerbation of environmental, social and cultural impacts in avocado-producing territories. The industry has promoted strategies that seek to legitimize production through the discourse of good business practices and sustainable certification processes. This strategy detracts attention from the physical-natural transformations and economic, social, cultural and political conflicts associated with expanded avocado production. In this context, the objective of this paper is to analyze how the central discourses of narratives on sustainability in the avocado industry create spaces for the reproduction and accumulation of capital. Based on the approaches of ethical value networks and metabolic rift, a comparative analysis of two case studies in conducted for Uruapan, Michoac & aacute;n in Mexico and Quillota-La Cruz, Valparaiso in Chile. The results show that both case studies present socio-economic deficiencies, with significant losses of vegetation cover, alterations in the hydrological cycle and soil erosion problems, which are invisible in the narrative on sustainability being upheld by the industry, thus exacerbating the metabolic rift of society-nature relations.||The increase in avocado consumption produces the expansion of the areas occupied by monoculture and the exacerbation of environmental impacts that show the obsolescence of the sustainable certification strategies adopted by the industry. The theoretical analysis addresses the networks of ethical value and the metabolic fracture from which the legitimation of the product is sought from the discourse of sustainable production while making invisible the physical-natural transformations and economic, social, cultural and political conflicts. The objective is to discuss the discourses of sustainability in avocado production with the postulates of ethical value networks based on the analysis of four dimensions: industry, justice, sustainability and geographical origin. To this end, the cases of Uruapan, Michoacán in Mexico and Quillota-La Cruz, Valparaíso in Chile are analyzed. It is concluded that both case studies have socioeconomic shortcomings, with significant losses of vegetation cover, alterations in the hydrological cycle and soil erosion problems in which the metabolic crack of society-nature relations deepens."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""12/23/2025"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.12775/bgss-2025-0031"", """", """", """", ""2083-8298"", """", """", """", """", """", ""1732-4254"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""https://doi.org/10.12775/bgss-2025-0031||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/420053"", """", ""WOS:001586857800002"", """", ""No Informado; Rodríguez Leiva, Sebastian Igor; 0000-0002-7063-0177; 196716||Instituto de Geografía; Hidalgo Dattwyler, Rodrigo Alejandro; 0000-0001-6092-1547; 89195"", """", ""69"", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", ""contenido completo"", """", ""128"", """", ""117"", """", """", """", """", """", ""NICOLAUS COPERNICUS UNIV TORUN"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""BULLETIN OF GEOGRAPHY-SOCIO-ECONOMIC SERIES"", """", """", """", ""Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License"", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", ""https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""01 No poverty||08 Decent work and economic growth||12 Responsible consumption and production"", """", ""01 Fin de la pobreza||08 Trabajo decente y crecimiento económico||12 Producción y consumo responsables"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""metabolic rift||ethical value networks||sustainability||deforestracion||avocado||Mexico||Chile"", """", """", """", """", ""Ethical value networks, metabolic rift and sustainability in Mexican and Chilean avocado production. The cases of Uruapan and Quillota-La Cruz||Ethical value networks, metabolic fracture and sustainability in avocado production in Mexico and Chile. The cases of Uruapan and Quillota - La Cruz"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Ethical value networks, metabolic rift and sustainability in Mexican and Chilean avocado production. The cases of Uruapan and Quillota-La Cruz||Ethical value networks, metabolic fracture and sustainability in avocado production in Mexico and Chile. The cases of Uruapan and Quillota - La Cruz"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""69"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""196716||89195"", """", ""12/23/2025"", """", """", """", ""2026-07-19;196716;1||2025-12-23;89195;1"", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS_ID: KYD-1786-2024||WOS_ID: ONN-1256-2025||WOS_ID: DVT-7870-2022||WOS_ID: CDY-1891-2022||WOS_ID: ONQ-0482-2025"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS"", """", """", """", """", """", ""WOS;2026-03-20"", """", """", ""Sin validar||Validado"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2026-07-19;196716;1||2025-12-23;89195;1"", """"]","[""de19f93c-2a44-4450-87b3-77fe39a44aff"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Rodríguez Leiva, Sebastián||Rodríguez, Norma Angélica||Hidalgo, Rodrigo||Vieyra, Antonio||Montes, Octavio"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2025-12-16T00:25:34Z"", """", ""2025-12-16T00:25:34Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2025"", """", """", """", """", """", ""The increase in avocado consumption produces the expansion of the areas occupied by monoculture and the exacerbation of environmental impacts that show the obsolescence of the sustainable certification strategies adopted by the industry. The theoretical analysis addresses the networks of ethical value and the metabolic fracture from which the legitimation of the product is sought from the discourse of sustainable production while making invisible the physical-natural transformations and economic, social, cultural and political conflicts. The objective is to discuss the discourses of sustainability in avocado production with the postulates of ethical value networks based on the analysis of four dimensions: industry, justice, sustainability and geographical origin. To this end, the cases of Uruapan, Michoacán in Mexico and Quillota-La Cruz, Valparaíso in Chile are analyzed. It is concluded that both case studies have socioeconomic shortcomings, with significant losses of vegetation cover, alterations in the hydrological cycle and soil erosion problems in which the metabolic crack of society-nature relations deepens."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""12/23/2025"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""1732-4254"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""https://doi.org/10.12775/bgss-2025-0031||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/414928"", """", """", """", ""Instituto de Geografía; Hidalgo Dattwyler, Rodrigo Alejandro; 0000-0001-6092-1547; 89195"", """", ""69"", """", """", ""en"", """", """", """", """", """", ""contenido completo"", """", ""128"", """", ""117"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Bulletin of Geography: Socio-economic Series"", """", """", """", ""Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License"", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", ""https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""12 Responsible consumption and production"", """", ""12 Producción y consumo responsables"", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Metabolic rift||Ethical value networks||Sustainability||Deforestracion||Avocado||Mexico||Chile"", """", """", """", """", ""Ethical value networks, metabolic fracture and sustainability in avocado production in Mexico and Chile. The cases of Uruapan and Quillota - La Cruz"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Ethical value networks, metabolic fracture and sustainability in avocado production in Mexico and Chile. The cases of Uruapan and Quillota - La Cruz"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""89195"", """", ""12/23/2025"", """", """", """", ""2025-12-23;89195;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2025-12-23;89195;1"", """"]"
9c366aa2-9c85-4925-aca1-18b04c29808f,9d73d3f7-b6ac-4c99-bd5f-a6c389465eae,identifier,"doi; conflicts=yid,dc.identifier.uri",identifier_conflict,"[""9c366aa2-9c85-4925-aca1-18b04c29808f"", ""123456789/2"", """", """", """", """", ""jlo||carga"", """", """", """", """", ""González Aguero, Marcela Margot||Lucchini Raies, Camila||Márquez Doren, Francisca||Martínez Santana, Dayann Carolina||Osorio Leyton, Tatiana||Bozo Araya, Catalina||Castillo-Valenzuela, Isabel||Parra Venegas, Andrea||Catoni Salamanca, María Isabel||Gonzalez-Aguero M.||Lucchini-Raies C.||Marquez-Doren F.||Santana D.M.||Leyton T.O.||Araya C.B.||Valenzuela I.C.||Venegas A.P.||Salamanca M.I.C."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""2026-01-12T12:06:15Z||2026-03-22T14:49:48Z"", """", ""2026-01-12T12:06:15Z||2026-03-22T14:49:48Z"", """", """", """", """", ""2025"", """", """", """", """", """", ""INTRODUCCIÓN. En América del Sur solo Uruguay y Paraguay han avanzado en la caracterización de su personal de enfermería. Chile no cuenta con estudios al respecto. La disponibilidad de datos es clave para orientar políticas laborales y formativas. OBJETIVO. Describir la situación de la enfermería profesional y técnica en Chile en cuanto a aspectos sociodemográficos, de formación, laborales y de salud. MÉTODOS. Estudio cuantitativo, descriptivo, transversal con diseño muestral no probabilístico por bola de nieve, dirigido al personal de enfermería del país. Se aplicó una encuesta autoadministrada vía web. El análisis se realizó mediante estadística descriptiva incluyendo distribución de frecuencia, porcentajes y prueba de X2 para comparaciones. RESULTADOS. Respondieron la encuesta 8.348 personas, 74% enfermeras/os profesionales y 26% técnicos de enfermería. Los resultados muestran que un 88% del personal de enfermería es de sexo femenino, 72% tiene entre 20 y 40 años, 67% trabaja en el sector público, 37% cuenta con contrato indefinido y 61% presenta al menos una licencia médica en los últimos 12 meses. En el personal técnico se observa mayor precariedad laboral. CONCLUSIONES. Este estudio representa la primera aproximación al estado de la enfermería chilena, develando la escasa información disponible acerca de este grupo, especialmente sobre los técnicos. Para comprender la situación del personal de enfermería en el largo plazo, es preciso contar con un modelo de información sobre recursos humanos que sea sistemático, de alcance nacional y acceso libre, capturando así desafíos y diferencias regionales. Queda pendiente profundizar el estudio cualitativo de las brechas de género.||© 2025, Escuela de Enfermeria Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Chile. All rights reserved.INTRODUCTION. In South America, only Uruguay and Paraguay have made progress in characterizing their nursing staff. Chile does not have studies on this matter. The availability of data is key to guiding labor and training policies. OBJECTIVE. To describe the situation of professional and technical nursing in Chile regarding sociodemographic, educational, labor, and health aspects. METHODS. Quantitative, descriptive, cross-sectional study with a non-probabilistic snowball sampling design, aimed at the country’s nursing staff. A self-administered web survey was applied. Analysis was conducted using descriptive statistics, including frequency distribution, percentages, and Chi-square tests for comparisons. RESULTS. 8,348 people responded to the survey, 74% professional nurses and 26% nursing technicians. The results show that 88% of the nursing staff are female, 72% are between 20 and 40 years old, 67% work in the public sector, 37% have a permanent contract, and 61% have had at least one medical leave in the past 12 months. Greater job insecurity is observed among technical staff. CONCLUSIONS. This study represents the first approach to the state of Chilean nursing, revealing the limited information available about this group, especially regarding technicians. To understand the long-term situation of nursing staff, it is necessary to have a human resources information model that is systematic, nationwide, and freely accessible, thereby capturing regional challenges and differences. Further qualitative study on gender gaps remains pending."", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""1/20/2026"", """", """", ""10 páginas"", """", """", """", ""ORCID||SCOPUS"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""10.7764/Horiz_Enferm.36.3.1020-1029"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""0716-8861"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""SCOPUS_ID:105028285657"", """", ""https://doi.org/10.7764/Horiz_Enferm.36.3.1020-1029||https://sipa.uc.cl/handle/123456789/415847"", """", """", """", ""Escuela de Enfermería; González Aguero, Marcela Margot; S/I; 119783||Escuela de Enfermería; Lucchini Raies, Camila; 0000-0001-5704-9778; 18598||Escuela de Enfermería; Márquez Doren, Francisca; 0000-0001-8093-4687; 8328||Escuela de Enfermería; Martínez Santana, Dayann Carolina; 0000-0002-2504-2587; 141576||Escuela de Enfermería; Osorio Leyton, Tatiana Paz; 0000-0003-3980-595X; 205582||Escuela de Enfermería; Bozo Araya, Catalina; S/I; 223713||Escuela de Enfermería; Lucchini Raies, Camila Estefania; 0000-0001-5704-9778; 18598||Escuela de Enfermería; Marquez Doren, Francisca Andrea; 0000-0001-8093-4687; 8328||Escuela de Enfermería; Osorio Leyton, Tatiana Paz; S/I; 205582||No Informado; Bozo Araya, Catalina Concepción; S/I; 223713||Escuela de Enfermería; Isabel Margarita Castillo Valenzuela; S/I; 226343||Escuela de Enfermería; Catoni Salamanca, Maria Isabel; 0009-0006-0131-365X; 637"", """", """", """", """", ""es||spa"", """", """", """", """", """", ""contenido completo"", """", ""1029"", """", ""1020"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Escuela de Enfermeria Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Chile"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Horizonte de Enfermería"", """", """", """", ""CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International"", """", ""acceso abierto"", """", ""https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""610"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Enfermeras y Enfermeros||Fuerza Laboral en Salud||Condiciones de Trabajo||América Latina||Gender||Health Workforce||Latin America||Nurses||Working Conditions"", """", """", """", """", ""Situación del personal de enfermería chileno en 2023: estudio preliminar||THE STATE OF THE CHILEAN NURSING WORKFORCE IN 2023: LESSONS FOR THE AMERICASSITUACIÓN DEL PERSONAL DE ENFERMERÍA CHILENO EN 2023: ESTUDIO PRELIMINAR"", """", """", ""The State of the Chilean nursing workforce in 2023: lessons for the Americas"", """", """", ""Situación del personal de enfermería chileno en 2023: estudio preliminar||THE STATE OF THE CHILEAN NURSING WORKFORCE IN 2023: LESSONS FOR THE AMERICASSITUACIÓN DEL PERSONAL DE ENFERMERÍA CHILENO EN 2023: ESTUDIO PRELIMINAR"", ""artículo"", """", """", """", """", """", ""36"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""119783||18598||8328||141576||205582||223713||226343||637"", """", ""1/20/2026"", """", """", """", ""2026-01-20;119783;1||2026-01-20;18598;1||2026-01-20;8328;1||2026-01-20;141576;1||2026-01-20;205582;1||2026-01-20;223713;1||2026-07-01;119783;1||2026-07-01;18598;1||2026-07-01;8328;1||2026-07-01;141576;1||2026-07-01;205582;1||2026-07-01;223713;1||2026-07-01;226343;1||2026-07-01;637;1"", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", """", ""Scopus"", """", """", """", """", """", ""ORCID;2026-01-12||SCOPUS;2026-03-22"", """", """", ""Validado||Sin validar"", """", """", """", """", """", ""Validado"", """", ""2026-01-20;119783;1||2026-01-20;18598;1||2026-01-20;8328;1||2026-01-20;141576;1||2026-01-20;205582;1||2026-01-20;223713;1||2026-